{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares","id":540642,"title":"Homebrew Nightmares","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-04T23:06:08-07:00","id":540642,"title":"Homebrew Nightmares","content":"Because, surprisingly, there wasn't already a thread for this, even though Nightmares are literally designed to be homebrewed. Here until we get a Beast forum. Ideas or fully crunched mechanics are both fine, as are Nightmares based on homebrew templates.<br /> <br /> You Are Not Prepared (General): The nightmare of showing up naked to class, or having to take a test you didn't study for, all part of the wider fear of not being prepared. Most likely makes the target more likely to neglect crucial items or preparations.<br /> <br /> You Are Not Good Enough (General): The target becomes convinced of their own weakness, but instead tries to compensate for it with excessive training, to the point of doing much more harm than good. They also become obsessed with anything that could give them &quot;an edge&quot;, to the point of seeking out vampires and begging to be embraced or ghouled or volunteering for bizarre mad science experiments.<br /> <br /> It's a Jungle Out There (Often Vampire, but can come from any politically vicious monster): The target becomes convinced that the world is hostile, uncaring, and mercilessly Darwinian, and comes to believe that only be stamping out all compassion and being as ruthless as possible can they raise their station. <br /> <br /> Curiosity Killed the Cat (Guardian of the Veil Mage): The target becomes convinced that any attempt to investigate bizarre or supernatural occurrences is incredibly dangerous, and will obsessively avoid anything unusual. <br /> <br /> You Are Obsolete (Free Council Mage, Genius): The target becomes a walking anachronism: they become hopeless with current technology, slang, and culture, utterly convinced that their own devices and knowledge are hopelessly out of date.<br /> <br /> Mind Your Manners (Chatelaine Changeling, True Fae): The target becomes scrupulous about adhering to various ancient and traditional rules of decorum: hospitality, honorable combat, and &quot;good form&quot; in general. <br /> <br /> Memories Are Fleeting (Mummy): The target forgets something important: a major event from their past, a friend or family member<br /> <br /> They Are Not Ready (Guardian of the Veil or Genius): The target becomes convinced that others, even their friends and allies, are unworthy of learning or incapable of grasping some type of &quot;forbidden knowledge&quot;, causing them to obsessively safeguard everything they know and learn, going so far as to conceal crucial information from their allies.<br /> <br /> You Could Wake Up Dead Tomorrow (Sin-Eater): &quot;Oh Bart, don't worry, people die all the time. In fact, you could wake up dead tomorrow.&quot;. No idea what it would do, I just couldn't resist. <br /> <br /> Anything Could Kill You (Forgotten Sin-Eater): The Beast can convince the target that a completely innocuous object, place, or situation is incredibly lethal. <br /> <br /> You Know Nothing (Genius): The victim's Mental attributes and skills cease to work as they become convinced that all they know is infinitely inferior to others, and that the laws of the world are far too vast to ever be understood by their puny mind. <br /> <br /> Dead Timeline (Lemurian Genius, possibly any Genius or Mage involved with time travel): The target becomes convinced that they have time traveled in some way: to the past, future, or another timeline.<br /> <br /> Pseudoscience (Unmada Genius): The target becomes convinced that some law of physics or scientific fact is false, and their own pet theory is true. This causes them to, for example, believe that any device that operates based on laws contrary to their own beliefs does not work. <br /> <br /> You'll Kill Us All! (Klagen Genius): The target becomes convinced that one of their projects or endeavors will almost certainly end in chaos and tragedy. <br /> <br /> Kill to Know (Mysterium Mage, Staunen Genius, Mekhet Vampire...the list goes on.): The target becomes obsessed with answering a question or solving a certain mystery, regardless of how difficult or dangerous it is. <br /> <br /> If Only You Ruled The World (Hoffnung Genius, any monster with utopian plans and megalomania): The target begins to believe that they could solve all the world's problems, if only they were in charge. They will refuse to yield any power or leadership positions they have, and will insist that everyone else follows their decisions, becoming sullen or violent if not obeyed. <br /> <br /> They Called You Mad (Neid Genius): I have a few ideas, but my favorite one is that it forces the target into stereotypical &quot;mad scientist&quot; behavior.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T23:15:56-07:00","id":540663,"title":"","content":"Here's the first draft of one I made for Strix Kinship.<br /> <br /> <b>No Masks For You </b>[Strix Kinship]<br /> <i>You can't hide who, or what, you really are anymore. All masks are stripped away, all lies stand revealed, and you can hardly remember why they were there in the first place. Then you come back to yourself, and are left to face what people feel about the real you - if anyone is left when you're done.</i><br /> <b>Dicepool</b>: Wits + Satiety vs Composure + Supernatural Tolerance<br /> <b>Normal Satiety:</b> The victim loses the benefits of all forms of disguise whether it be from make-up, costume, or a vampire's Blush of Life. It cannot overcome more potent forms of obscuring physical identity, however; powers such as Obfuscate, or passive disguises like a Changeling's Mien or a Mummy's Sahu will not so much as flicker at this level.<br /> <br /> <b>High Satiety:</b> Even spoken lies and partial truths are beyond the victim's ability to manage; they fail all social rolls to deceive others. The only way they can keep a secret is to refrain from communication, which can have consequences of its own. This may be overcome for a turn by spending a point of Willpower, but such a measure will not protect them from continued questioning.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> The victim cannot regain Willpower from their Virtue, and must spend Willpower to resist any provocation or opportunity to fulfill their Vice. Supernatural beings without Virtue or Vice lose access to whichever replacement they have that reflects a connection to or facade of humanity (Life, Masks, Bone, etc.), and must spend Willpower to resist that which reflects their monstrous self (Legend, Dirge, Blood, etc.).<br /> <br /> With Satiety expenditure the Normal effect's limitations briefly disappear. Things as a Changeling's Mien, a Mummy's Sahu, or active powers of disguise such as the vampire Obfuscate Discipline falter for a turn against a successful use at this level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T23:23:54-07:00","id":540684,"title":"","content":"Cool!<br /> <br /> Rumpelstiltskin Syndrome (Mage or Changeling): The target temporarily gains a &quot;true name&quot;. It will be a name they have used before, but not the one they use: their full name, a childhood nickname, an alias they once used, or so on. They are compelled to obey anyone who knows this name for as long as the Nightmare lasts.<br /> <br /> Ow The Edge (Belial's Brood Vampire, various Left-Hand Paths, etc.): The target becomes convinced that conventions and morals are just cages, and that they must break those boundaries to shock others into understanding. Or something. Basically, the target becomes an insufferable prick who ignores social graces and decency for the hell of it, causing them to lose access to Social attributes, skills, and merits due to their profound unpleasance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 06-05-2015, 02:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T23:50:06-07:00","id":540719,"title":"","content":"<b>Better Off Without You: </b>(Promethean)<br /> <b>Step 1: </b>Nature of the Fear (You aren't good enough, all you do is hurt the people you care about, <i>[From doubt in the Pilgrimage]</i>)<br /> <b>Step 2:</b><ul><li>Normal Effect: Inflicts the Resigned Condition. (See WtF 2nd ed)</li> <li>High Satiety: Also Inflicts the Guilty Condition</li> <li>Satiety Expenditure: Compels the Target to abandon their allies; picking up stakes and move on before anyone else nearby suffers.</li> </ul><br /> <b>Step 3: </b>Manipulation (foolish behaviour) or Wits (self-doubt) + Satiety? Not sure; vs Resolve (erodes self confidence) + Supernatural Tolerence<br /> <b>Step 4:</b> Ask the audience; is this too much?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":1624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","user":"FallenEco","date":". 06-05-2015, 05:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T06:52:56-07:00","id":541093,"title":"","content":"<b>Kneel Before Your God:</b> (Leviathan)<br /> The Leviathan's Wake is a potent tool, allowing them to dominate, terrify and control those around them.With practice, you too can bend the wills of those around you like your closest cousins.<br /> <b>Nature of the Fear:</b> Religious terror, the idea of something so powerful and ancient, the differences between it and a god is semantics, and it's not the kind of god <i>you</i> believe in.<br /> <b>Effects:</b><ul><li>Normal Effect: Inflicts the Shaken condition</li> <li>High Satiety: Also Inflicts the Awed Condition</li> <li>Satiety Expenditure: Inflicts the Broken Condition</li> </ul><b>Dice Pool:</b> Presence + Satiety - Composure + Supernatural Tolerance<br /> <br /> <b>Wrathful Storm:</b> (Princess)<br /> The Hopeful don't like Beasts. Nobility spend their lives trying to spark hope, destroy darkness, and fight fear. Beasts survive by inspiring despair, they live in nightmares, and they are literal personifications of fear. Despite this, Beasts still feel kinship with the Princes and Princesses of both Radiant and Twilight Queens. The Children of the Queen of Storms, however, have no problem working with Beasts if they prove themselves helpful against Darkspawn. The Begotten have learned to mimic the rage of the Queen of Storms, inciting it in normally harmless individuals.<br /> <b>Nature of the Fear:</b> Losing control and hurting those close to you.<ul><li>Normal Effect: The target becomes needlessly hostile to those around them, gaining the Enraged condition for a scene. Certain supernatural creatures may be affected differently:<ul><li>Vampires:A Vampire affected by this Nightmare goes into Frenzy.</li> <li>Werewolves: A Werewolf affected by this Nightmare enters soft Rage (<i>wasu-im</i>).</li> <li>Demons: This doesn't offer any specific effects against Demons, but could cause them to Compromise themselves, and if they suffer such a Compromise, they also gain the Shaken condition for the scene</li> <li>Sin-Eaters: The Geist takes control of the body for the scene, and acts out all their bizarre Geistly desires and compulsions.</li> <li>Promethean: The Promethean enters Torment when affected by this Nightmare.</li> </ul></li> <li>High Satiety: The target loses all sense. they can not be snapped out of the Enraged condition imposed by this Nightmare by others.</li> <li>Satiety Expenditure: The target gains the Rabid condition instead of Enraged.<ul><li>Vampires may not spend Willpower to hold off the Beast.</li> <li>Werewolves go straight to hard Rage (<i>basu-im</i>), skipping soft rage.</li> <li>Sin-Eaters suffer an immediate Breaking Point against Synergy, regardless of their actions.</li> <li>Prometheans snap, and go catatonic for the scene, pushed even past Torment.</li> </ul></li> </ul><br /> <b>Enraged (Condition)</b><br /> You are enraged about something, pushing you to the edge of your self-control, and making you far less capable of peaceable interaction. You suffer a -3 penalty to Composure and Resolve rolls, as well as rolls with Social skills (excluding Intimidation).<br /> <b>Resolution:</b> Kill or gravely injure somebody in a fit of rage, or be talked out of it by a friend (Expression + Manipulation + your Integrity - 10)<br /> <br /> <b>Rabid (Condition)</b><br /> You have completely lost it. You're a rabid dog, and if you don't stop soon, somebody may put you down. Unless you put them down first. You must attack anyone nearby, friend or foe, although you can choose specific targets if there's more than one creature around to attack. If you're alone (or believe yourself to be), you throw things, break things, and generally make a massive mess. On the upside, your attacks do deal +1 damage, as your incredible rage drives you to kill.<br /> <b>Resolution:</b> None. You just have to scream and snarl and rage until either you're too exhausted to keep doing it, or you come to your senses.<br /> <br /> <b>Doomed to Failure</b> (Genius)<br /> The Inspired are a sorry lot, especially compared to other Kin. Everything they try to do eventually ends in failure, and they can never be understood by the normal humans among which they once stood. Such a life can be misery for many Geniuses, especially those who can't find support from colleagues and Beholden. This pain fuels this Nightmare, which drives men mad with despair.<br /> <b>Nature of the Fear:</b> You're nothing, and nothing you ever do will matter.<ul><li>Normal Effect: The target feels the crushing weight of failure on their shoulders. Their next roll loses the 10-again quality (and the 9- and 8-again and rote qualities, if applicable).</li> <li>High Satiety: The target suffers the above, plus a penalty equal to 10 - Integrity.</li> <li>Satiety Expenditure: The target becomes completely inept. Reduce their next roll to a chance die (which keeps 10-again).</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T07:27:42-07:00","id":541150,"title":"","content":"<b>That Looks Infected</b> (Venombite Changeling)<br /> <i>Gee, buddy, I don't know what bit you, but that does not look good. You should really go get that checked out before it spreads. Might be too late; see that discoloration there? Yeah, there. I'd guess beriberi. Hey, maybe I'm wrong, maybe it's just tetanus. Anything's possible.</i><br /> To use this Nightmare, a victim must be suffering at least a single point of Bashing damage as the result of some kind of flesh wound.<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Manipulation + Satiety vs. Resolve + Supernatural Tolerance<br /> <b>Normal Satiety:</b> In the subject's eyes, the wound blossoms a sickly color, spreading across his skin. The fear of infection gives him the Shaken Condition.<br /> <b>High Satiety:</b> The parasite of the idea that his scratch is infected has buried its way so deep into the subject's mind, there's no escape. Until the target receives medical treatment, at the beginning of each scene, he gains the Shaken Condition if he does not already have it.<br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure: </b>The imaginary illness becomes psychosomatic. The target suffers from an appropriate Tilt of the Beast's choosing, such as Arm/Leg Wrack, Insane, or Sick. This lasts for as long as the target has the Shaken Condition.<br /> <b>Other Possible Kinships:</b> Blightbent Changeling, Morbus Vampire, Moros Mage, Thyrsus Mage, Mummy with Kiss of Apep, Stricken Sin-Eater, Were-cockroach","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T19:50:27-07:00","id":542048,"title":"","content":"Alright, here's my first try at this. Sorry if it sucks!<br /> <br /> <b>You Can't Quit Me</b>(Daeva)<br /> <br /> <i>You want to get away, to never see them again. But then they smile and whisper in your ear, and your heart turns in your chest and the wonderful warmth spreads through your flesh, and you know, deep down inside, that you'll never leave them, no matter how badly they hurt you.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Manipulation + Satiety vs Resolve + Supernatural Tolerance<br /> <br /> <b>Normal:</b> The victim gains the Swooning Condition (p. XX) keyed towards the Beast, and cannot resolve it during the scene, no matter how many times they bend to the Child's will. After the scene ends, the Condition may be resolved normally.<br /> <br /> <b>High Satiety:</b> As normal, save that the Beast treats their Impression level as two higher against the afflicted target, to a maximum of perfect(see p. XX).<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> The victim gains the Addicted(Persistent) Condition (p. XX),which does not resolve when the Nightmare ends and is keyed towards acts of kindness and affirmation(A kiss on the cheek, warm praise, a soft smile, anything of that sort will do) from the user.*<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> When resisting the user's mundane Social rolls, the victim gains an Exceptional Success on 6 Successes instead of 5.<br /> <br /> So, what do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T04:06:35-07:00","id":542428,"title":"","content":"<b>1st Draft of a Custom Nightmare, it's my first attempt at one... So it's a bit rough... I have yet to run a comparison check with it.<br /> <br /> <u>Eating You from the Inside Out</u></b>;<br /> <br /> <i>Why can't I ever get my fill? I'm eating but getting hungrier... It feels like something is inside me... It's growing bigger... It can't be because of 'that', can it?</i><br /> <br /> <b>Dicepool:</b> Manipulation or Wits + Satiety vs. Resolve/Stamina + Supernatural Tolerance.<br /> <br /> <b>Normal Effect</b>: The target gains the Guilty Condition, constantly distracted by the thought they are carrying a physical manifestation of some guilt inside them... Perhaps if they do some good turn, it'll go away? This Condition cannot be resolved whilst the Nightmare is active, only once it's effect has passed.<br /> <br /> <b>High Satiety:</b> The target's guilt based tape-worm actually feeds off them. Successes drain the equivalent in Willpower for Mortals or for supernaturals it drinks Vitae, Essence etc.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> As long as the Nightmare is in effect, the Beast may expend one Satiety to make the victim's next social roll becomes a chance roll as they become increasingly withdrawn over what they believe they're hosting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3951,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","user":"wander","date":". 06-08-2015, 05:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T10:38:30-07:00","id":545517,"title":"","content":"Here's a nightmare. You're a storyteller who's put hours upon hours into prepping for your next session, and you have players that do <a href=\"http://www.railsoff.com/2015/06/how-to-piss-off-your-dungeon-master.html\" target=\"_blank\">THIS</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6264-b-chaos","name":"B. Chaos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T11:55:28-07:00","id":545594,"title":"","content":"You Are Possessed(Strix)<br /> <br /> <i>Something else controls your body. You wouldn't have done those things. No, it was a demon, a monster in your skin. No matter how much you enjoyed it.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Wits + Satiety vs Composure + Supernatural Tolerance<br /> <br /> <b>Normal:</b> To the victim, they appear to be possessed, a prisoner in their own flesh. In actuality, their own inner demons have come out to play. The target gains the Wanton Condition(p. XX), which cannot be resolved until the Nightmare ends.<br /> <br /> <b>High Satiety:</b> The victim's belief that they are no longer responsible for their own actions reaches a new height. For the duration of the Nightmare, the victim does not (and cannot) suffer from breaking points due to his own actions. Things that would normally prompt breaking points (such as murder, theft, or assault, or even nonviolent acts that are nevertheless fundamentally opposed to the character\u2019s self-image) seem as reasonable and as appropriate as having a polite discussion. In addition to making the victim potentially act wildly out of character, this Nightmare negates any penalties to Social maneuvers or similar actions that might arise due to breaking points. It\u2019s as easy to convince the victim to murder his boss as it is to convince him to loan you his car.<br /> <br /> Once the Nightmare\u2019s duration ends, the victim must immediately roll for any and all actions undertaken during the Nightmare that would call for breaking points.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> For a target hit with this level of the Nightmare, their basest desires become paramount. For the duration of the Nightmare, the target must take any opportunity to indulge their Vice, <i>spending</i> a point of Willpower if they fail to do so.<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> The penalties of the Wanton Condition are raised from -2 to -4.<br /> <br /> Like my last one, this probably sucks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T12:16:47-07:00","id":545611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>B. Chaos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=545517#post545517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's a nightmare. You're a storyteller who's put hours upon hours into prepping for your next session, and you have players that do <a href=\"http://www.railsoff.com/2015/06/how-to-piss-off-your-dungeon-master.html\" target=\"_blank\">THIS</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>You Are in a Dark of Worldness</b> (God-Machine Kinship)<br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool</b>: 10-Integrity + Resolve vs Highest Integrity + Resolve in scene<br /> <br /> <b>Normal</b>: The Storyteller must write down the names of every person immediately visible in the scene and a minor detail about them and their favorite monster movie. Open two doors when making a Social Maneuvering roll against a character when a monster matching this movie is in the scene and reveals its nature to the character.<br /> <br /> <b>High Satiety</b>: A single individual in the scene gains a Major Template, either immediately or as soon as circumstances can be contrived to explain it. This individual may already have a Major Template, in which case the new one replaces their original, but they retain all the supernatural powers of their previous form. All normal human beings in the scene gain a Minor Template, chosen randomly for each.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure</b>: The Storyteller goes and selects the first roleplaying module they can find, WoD or otherwise, that is not the present one. Pick a random page in its progression. The Storyteller immediately talks through how the characters wind up in those circumstances and play resumes from there. The original scenario can not be returned to, even with further uses of this Nightmare.<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success</b>: The user puts away their character sheet. For the remainder of the Chapter, they roll according to how many dots they think they remember from their sheet. 1's now count as 10's because they look really similar and now its too late to change the outcome because it's been two whole turns, okay? Get off my back, man.<br /> <br /> (Forgive me; I had to. XD)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2320-tilting-clock","name":"Tilting Clock","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T16:47:59-07:00","id":547725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=542048#post542048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, here's my first try at this. Sorry if it sucks!<br /> <br /> <b>You Can't Quit Me</b>(Daeva)<br /> <br /> <i>You want to get away, to never see them again. But then they smile and whisper in your ear, and your heart turns in your chest and the wonderful warmth spreads through your flesh, and you know, deep down inside, that you'll never leave them, no matter how badly they hurt you.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Manipulation + Satiety vs Resolve + Supernatural Tolerance<br /> <br /> <b>Normal:</b> The victim gains the Swooning Condition (p. XX) keyed towards the Beast, and cannot resolve it during the scene, no matter how many times they bend to the Child's will. After the scene ends, the Condition may be resolved normally.<br /> <br /> <b>High Satiety:</b> As normal, save that the Beast treats their Impression level as two higher against the afflicted target, to a maximum of perfect(see p. XX).<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> The victim gains the Addicted(Persistent) Condition (p. XX),which does not resolve when the Nightmare ends and is keyed towards acts of kindness and affirmation(A kiss on the cheek, warm praise, a soft smile, anything of that sort will do) from the user.*<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> When resisting the user's mundane Social rolls, the victim gains an Exceptional Success on 6 Successes instead of 5.<br /> <br /> So, what do you think?</div> </div> </div> </div>I want this Nightmare. Deliciously horrifying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T04:47:08-07:00","id":548345,"title":"","content":"Oh, how about some kinship nightmares inspired by the translation guides? What nightmares might a Settite, Tzimisce, or Assamite inspire? Uktena or Get of Fenris? Euthanatos or Son of Ether?<br /> <br /> Also, there's a lot of untapped potential here, since nothing stops beasts from making kinship nightmares based on blue book stuff like spirits and ghosts, cutlists of things men weren't meant to know, skinchangers, slashers, demons and the possessed from inferno, and immortals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":391,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","user":"StSword","date":". 06-10-2015, 08:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T07:24:06-07:00","id":548527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=548345#post548345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, how about some kinship nightmares inspired by the translation guides? What nightmares might a Settite, Tzimisce, or Assamite inspire? Uktena or Get of Fenris? Euthanatos or Son of Ether?<br /> <br /> Also, there's a lot of untapped potential here, since nothing stops beasts from making kinship nightmares based on blue book stuff like spirits and ghosts, cutlists of things men weren't meant to know, skinchangers, slashers, demons and the possessed from inferno, and immortals.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <b>Gaia's Vengeance (old Werewolf)</b><br /> You hear a scrabbling sound in the shadows. A squeak or bark in the distance. The next thing you know, the creatures of nature are upon you. You can't escape mother Earth on foot, but you'd better still run.<br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Presence + Animal Ken vs. Composure + Supernatural Tolerance<br /> <b>Normal:</b> Animals become irritable toward the target, imposing the Earth Spurned Condition for the scene.<br /> <b>High Satiety:</b> The target instead receives the Earth Abandoned Condition.<br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> Instead of the above conditions, the target is simply attacked on sight by any animals they encounter for the rest of the scene.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> The effects above also extend to plants, fungi, and all forms of nature spirit. In the case of satiety expenditure, plants actually become animate and attack! Treat them as having Power equal to their Size + 1, Finesse of 5 - size (minimum 1), and Resistance equal to the greater of the Beast's Presence or the plant's Size rating. Health is Resistance + Size, Willpower is Resistance + Finesse, and Speed is 0 (although some plants, such as potted plants, may be able to drag themselves). Penalties to rolls to deal with non-animals are applied to whatever skill seems most appropriate to the Storyteller.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Earth Spurned:</b><br /> You and nature can't seem to get along right now. Your dog is being a jerk, a rat stole your lunch, and the neighbor's cats have been staring at you all day.<br /> <b>Effect:</b> You have difficulty influencing animals, receiving a -2 penalty to Animal Ken rolls.<br /> <b>Resolution:</b> Achieve an Exceptional Success or Dramatic Failure on an Animal Ken roll.<br /> <br /> <b>Earth Abandoned:</b><br /> It's just gotten worse. Your dog bit you for no reason, the rat that stole your lunch yesterday brought a bunch of friends, and your parrot has been calling you severely hurtful names all day.<br /> <b>Effect:</b> You just can't seem to get along with any sort of animal. Any Animal Ken rolls are reduced to a Chance Die, and nearby animals become agitated in your presence.<br /> <b>Resolution:</b> Accrue total Lethal damage in excess of your Stamina as a result of failed Animal Ken rolls.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>An Offer You Can't Refuse (Giovanni, Old Vampire)</b><br /> The deal this man is offering is clearly a bad idea, and you're obviously getting the raw end of it, but you're deperate. And, for some reason, you're feeling even more desperate with each passing moment.<br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Manipulation + Subterfuge - (Resolve + Supernatural Tolerance)<br /> <b>Normal:</b> You gain the benefit of Soft Leverage, a Vice, or an Aspiration against a target during the next Social Maneuvering attempt against them this scene, regardless of whether you actually have it.<br /> <b>High Satiety:</b> You may pick two of the above benefits to apply.<br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> You gain the benefits of Hard Leverage, placing psychic pressure on them. This Hard Leverage doesn't create extra doors.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> In your next Social Maneuvering attempt with the target this scene, reduce the number of doors by your Presence, minimum 1.<br /> <br /> <b>The Consensus is False (Old Mage)</b><br /> They think they're so smart, but you know the truth. They can't keep you down any longer, not with all the money, manpower, and phony papers in the world. Your truths will win out, consequences be damned.<br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Manipulation + 10 - (Integrity + Composure)<br /> <b>Normal:</b> The target becomes consumed with a need to prove themselves correct, regardless of if they actually are. They receive the Obsession condition for the scene, centered around proving that some delusion they hold is true, usually an incorrect scientific theory (the sun orbiting the Earth, luminiferous ether, etc.).<br /> <b>High Satiety:</b> The obsession is particularly consuming, imposing a -2 penalty to all rolls not relating to the target's Obsession, in addition to the effects ofthe Obsession condition.<br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> The condition imposed by the normal effect remains after the scene ends.<br /> <br /> <b>The Shadow Whispers (Wraith)</b><br /> In Jungian psychology, there's an idea called the Shadow Aspect, the part of your mind that you don't want to acknowledge. All your evils and weaknesses, all your failings and faults. And it won't shut up.<br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Manipulation + Academics - Integrity/Integrity equivalent<br /> <b>Normal:</b> The target is plagued by whispers that tempt away from the good in them. The target gains no benefits from their Virtue. In the case of Vampires, this instead extend to the Mask, and for Werewolves it affects the Bone if at high Harmony, or Blood at low Harmony. Bonuses that would normally come from these do not apply, and Willpower can not be regained from acting on them.<br /> <b>High Satiety:</b> The target s overcome with shock and shame over the things going through their head. If the target acts on their Vice (or their Dirge, or whichever Werewolf trait was not disabled), they receive a condition as if they failed a Breaking Point, regardless of if a Breaking Point occurred.<br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> The Shadow Aspect becomes aggressive, pushing its hardest to act on base urges. If acting on any of the traits mentioned in the High Satiety effect, they refill their Willpower completely, and any bonuses from acting on them are increased by +1.<br /> <br /> <b>Encroaching Banality (Old Changeling)</b><br /> Wake up. Brush your teeth. Get dressed. Get some coffee. Go to work. Come home. Kiss the wife. Have a cocktail. Eat dinner. Go to bed. Do it all again tomorrow. Do you remember what you ate yesterday? Do you remember where you were? Was it just an average day? Like every day you ever had? Every day you ever will have? Enjoy that illusion while you can.<br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Manipulation + Target's (Composure - Wits)<br /> <b>Normal:</b> The target is overcome with banality and skepticism, becoming incapable of believing in anything fantastical. While this makes them insufferable to watch TV with, it also makes them far better at forgetting or dismissing supernatural happening. The target receives a +2 bonus on Breaking Point rolls in response to a supernatural happening, but may not attempt any feat that they know is supernatural in nature.<br /> <b>High Satiety:</b> The target is utterly banal, sticking to a routine and lacking any creativity. Anything they do regularly in the course of an <i>average</i> day becomes a rote action, and anything else loses the 10-again quality on rolls for it.<br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> The target suffers total disbelief, and the weird and supernatural simply don't register. The next Breaking Point the target would suffer is totally ignored, and the target has no memory of it. If forced to remember, it could still incur another Breaking Point.<br /> <br /> <b>Imbued Immunity (Old Hunter)</b><br /> Your humanity asserts itself against the world of darkness, whether you want it or not. Claws dull, fire is dampened, and senses are dulled.<br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Presence + Occult vs. Resolve + Supernatural Tolerance<br /> <b>Normal:</b> The target is made human for a time, disabling some of their powers. Any hereditary or biological supernatural powers, as well as powers related to physical form, such as physical Disciplines, Werewolf shapeshifting, and Atavisms, are disabled for the scene. They appear to be entirely human, and have no detectable physical differences (Vampires lose their sunlight vulnerability and benefit from <i>blush of life</i>, Prometheans no longer have disfigurements, etc.)<br /> <b>High Satiety:</b> The target's purely supernatural abilities become more difficult to access, imposing a -2 penalty to the activation rolls for any supernatural powers not disabled by the normal effect. On the upside, however, they also are better able to resist the mystical downsides of their supernatural state. Add 2 dice to pools to resist or negate non-physical harmful effects from supernatural templates and merits, including resisting Frenzy, exiting Rage, and avoiding Torment and Disquiet, among other things.<br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> The target's supernatural powers of any stripe are completely suppressed. The non-physical powers can be reactivated for a turn with a Reflexive Resolve + Composure roll each turn, penalized by the invoking Beast's Lair.<br /> <br /> <b>God's Not Here (Old Demon)</b><br /> God has abandoned this world. It's not just something that old bigots say when they hear gays getting rights. It's true. That &quot;angel&quot; that just saved your granny's life? You don't want to know what it really was. Seriously.<br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Intelligence + Occult - (Resolve + Supernatural Tolerance)<br /> <b>Normal:</b> The target is struck with supernatural terror, realizing exactly how little anything is looking after them, and how much there is to protect them from. The target may not expend Willpower to gain extra dice on rolls. Devout Atheists are not immune or resistant to this Nightmare, as it pertains more closely to their sense of security than to a literal &quot;God&quot; figure's presence.<br /> <b>High Satiety:</b> The target can feel the demons and devils closing in. They receive the Panicked condition.<br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> The target sees demons everywhere, and is incapable of distinguishing between reality and their own fevered paranoia. The target gains the Paranoid condition.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> The target's concept of reality is utterly shattered. They must roll for a Breaking Point, penalized at -2. Instead of receiving the Guilty, Shaken or Spooked conditions, they receive a non-persistent version of Broken instead.<br /> <br /> <b>Shattered Soul (Old Mummy)</b><br /> You think you're all one piece, a single chunk of person that runs autonomously as a single unit. Even at the most literal level, that's bullshit. You're a bag of organs and bones and muscle and sinew and nerves, and they don't even work well together half the time. The front half of your brain is fighting with the back half, your immune system can turn on you at any time. The same is true of your soul. It's in a half dozen pieces, which don't agree on anything.<br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Manipulation + Empathy - (Composure + Supernatural Tolerance)<br /> <b>Normal:</b> A random piece of the target's soul (Ab, Ba, Ka, Ren or Sheut) is temporarily shattered off, becoming its own personality with its own goals. This shard controls a single arm or leg of the target. In order to make the limb act in concert during a given turn, the target has to make a Composure + Persuasion or Intimidation roll, subtracting one of their other Attributes based on the specific soul piece. If the roll fails, the target suffers the Arm Wrack or Leg Wrack tilt for that turn, depending on the limb in question.<ul><li><b>Ab:</b> Resolve; acts impulsively and emotionally</li> <li><b>Ba:</b> Wits; Rational, but extremely stubborn</li> <li><b>Ka:</b> Intelligence; Aggressive</li> <li><b>Ren:</b> Presence; Acts in self-preservation</li> <li><b>Sheut:</b> Manipulation; Violently insane</li> </ul><b>High Satiety:</b> You may choose which piece of the soul is splintered off, <i>or</i> which limb is controlled by the fragment.<br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> You split <i>two</i> pieces of the soul off, and if at High Satiety, you may select the soul fragment type or controlled limb independently for each.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> You split off two pieces of the soul, stacking with the Satiety expenditure effect to a total of three. If at High Satiety, you may select the soul fragment type or controlled limb independently for each (for all three if you are spending Satiety <i>and</i> have High Satiety, you fiend).<br /> <br /> <br /> I'll think of more later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":4488,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","user":"malonkey1","date":". 07-01-2015, 01:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T01:08:26-07:00","id":549876,"title":"","content":"Oh I thought of an idea for a Reaper based Nightmare-<br /> <br /> Immortality Ends- The target is incapable of healing the wounds from the demon's attacks for the rest of the scene.<br /> <br /> Some possible modifiers- Extra wound penalties, converting lethal to agg damage,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T20:57:58-07:00","id":553748,"title":"","content":"<b>All Water is Blood</b><br /> <i>Like the water in Lough Derg shed by the she-dragon</i><b>, </b><i>Caor\u00e1nach, all water becomes blood.</i><br /> <b>Dicepool</b>: Manipulation + Satiety vs Composure + Supernatural Tolerance<br /> <b>Normal Satiety:</b> All water until the end of the scene to target character appears to be blood. Be in rain water, lake water, or drinking water all water is blood to them.<br /> <br /> <b>High Satiety:</b> Even tears, saliva, and other clear bodily fluids are now blood for the end of the next scene.<br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> The target gets the Sickened Tilt.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6109,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6109-imposterzilla","user":"imposterzilla","date":". 06-14-2015, 12:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6109-imposterzilla","name":"imposterzilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6109_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T22:08:05-07:00","id":553882,"title":"","content":"Hmm. have you considered giving the beast the ability to make it rain blood with high satiety? <br /> <br /> I mean if it wasn't raining before. I mean sure tears of blood is as thing, but hardly seems as impressive as say making it rain blood in doors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T22:59:06-07:00","id":553949,"title":"","content":"A few ideas I had<br /> <br /> <b>I Need This </b>(Daeva) - The Beast inflicts an addiction on the target, shaped by the Beast's own Hunger. It can be for a person's presence, a consumable substance, the thrill of a specific action, etc.<br /> <br /> <b>Curse of Cassandra </b>(Acanthus) - inflicted on those who know too much, this assures that no one will believe them<br /> <br /> <b>It Must Be Finished </b>(Deceived) - the victim is overwhelmed by artistic inspiration and recieves substantial bonuses toward their work, however literally everything else receives equally large penalties as their art drains and consumes them<br /> <br /> <br /> I think a previous blog entry mentioned <b>You Cannot Stop </b>as an idea for Forgotten Sin-Eaters with car crash associations. I now that that (driving a car... often from the back seat? and not having any real control) is a recurring nightmare for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 06-14-2015, 02:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T10:31:24-07:00","id":554561,"title":"","content":"I wonder about cross application of Kinship. I mean, can't kinship with a Fire-Touched Werewolf, or a Stricken Sin-Eater also potential allow a Beast to learn &quot;You Are Infected&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T11:28:47-07:00","id":554616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=554561#post554561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder about cross application of Kinship. I mean, can't kinship with a Fire-Touched Werewolf, or a Stricken Sin-Eater also potential allow a Beast to learn &amp;quot;You Are Infected&amp;quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div> I believe this is called out as the case right before it shows the Kinship Nightmares.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T20:30:18-07:00","id":555155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=540663#post540663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's the first draft of one I made for Strix Kinship.<br /> <br /> <b>No Masks For You </b>[Strix Kinship]<br /> <i>You can't hide who, or what, you really are anymore. All masks are stripped away, all lies stand revealed, and you can hardly remember why they were there in the first place. Then you come back to yourself, and are left to face what people feel about the real you - if anyone is left when you're done.</i><br /> <b>Dicepool</b>: Wits + Satiety vs Composure + Supernatural Tolerance<br /> <b>Normal Satiety:</b> The victim loses the benefits of all forms of disguise whether it be from make-up, costume, or a vampire's Blush of Life. It cannot overcome more potent forms of obscuring physical identity, however; powers such as Obfuscate, or passive disguises like a Changeling's Mien or a Mummy's Sahu will not so much as flicker at this level.<br /> <br /> <b>High Satiety:</b> Even spoken lies and partial truths are beyond the victim's ability to manage; they fail all social rolls to deceive others. The only way they can keep a secret is to refrain from communication, which can have consequences of its own. This may be overcome for a turn by spending a point of Willpower, but such a measure will not protect them from continued questioning.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> The victim cannot regain Willpower from their Virtue, and must spend Willpower to resist any provocation or opportunity to fulfill their Vice. Supernatural beings without Virtue or Vice lose access to whichever replacement they have that reflects a connection to or facade of humanity (Life, Masks, Bone, etc.), and must spend Willpower to resist that which reflects their monstrous self (Legend, Dirge, Blood, etc.).<br /> <br /> With Satiety expenditure the Normal effect's limitations briefly disappear. Things as a Changeling's Mien, a Mummy's Sahu, or active powers of disguise such as the vampire Obfuscate Discipline falter for a turn against a successful use at this level.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love this one, but why Strix? What's the connection there?<br /> <br /> Actually it might make a good general one based on nightmares of being exposed (aka showing up somewhere naked).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T18:39:15-07:00","id":556347,"title":"","content":"Just ideas I had, not sure what mechanics it would have;<br /> <br /> <b>You are a Chair</b> (Changeling Kinship)<br /> <i>You realise you cannot move, though you're not bound in anyway, your limbs just won't move when you tell them. Then you realise you're contorted into a shape. It's uncomfortable and you can't get out of it. It's only when you look around and take in your surroundings, that you realise you're a piece of furniture now to whoever did this to you...</i><br /> <br /> <b>Constraining Chains</b> (Ogre Changeling kinship)<br /> <i>You awaken somewhere, a dank dungeon, a basement with rust covered walls... It's hard to tell. You got to leave and realise you've been bound to the wall. Then 'It' comes and you know you have to get away... You tug at the bonds, but they don't break... They seem to get tougher... And at the same time, they're cutting into your flesh... It hurts but you need to get away... Until you realise the chains are slicing into your flesh and ripping through bone much worse than however 'That Thing' could do so...</i><br /> <br /> <b>Unending Work</b> (Wizened Changeling kinship)<br /> <i>You're linked to a workbench and forced into work, perhaps repairing a small pile of items. It doesn't seem too bad - at first, but for every item repaired it seems two or more take it's place. The pile grows larger for every item fixed and soon a supervisor comes and announces you're not working fast enough. You try but the pile keeps growing and soon the supervisor is using harsh words, threats to loved ones, they whip and cajole and cause you pain and the only way they'll stop is when you finish but the pile just keeps getting bigger...</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T19:48:06-07:00","id":556401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=556347#post556347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just ideas I had, not sure what mechanics it would have;<br /> <br /> <b>You are a Chair</b> (Changeling Kinship)<br /> <i>You realise you cannot move, though you're not bound in anyway, your limbs just won't move when you tell them. Then you realise you're contorted into a shape. It's uncomfortable and you can't get out of it. It's only when you look around and take in your surroundings, that you realise you're a piece of furniture now to whoever did this to you...</i></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://romanticallyapocalyptic.com/blog/shoe\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://romanticallyapocalyptic.com/blog/shoe\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://romanticallyapocalyptic.com/blog/shoe\" target=\"_blank\"> http://romanticallyapocalyptic.com/blog/shoe </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T21:23:30-07:00","id":556499,"title":"","content":"No One Walks Here (hunters in darkness) - imbues a location with a fearsome aura that creates rumors guaranteeing MOST people won't dare violate your territory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T22:32:31-07:00","id":556553,"title":"","content":"All According to Plan (Genius Slashers): Your target's actions always end up working in your favor.<br /> <br /> Somebody Else's Death (Abmortals, Sin-Eaters): Prevent one target from dying at the expense of another character's life<br /> <br /> Dust to Dust (Immortals): Your target becomes decrepit and ancient-feeling, making them physically feeble but granting them ancient knowledge<br /> <br /> Soaked in Blood (Blood Bathers): Your target believes themself to be covered in blood and viscera, and feels compelled to clean themselves, possibly scrubbing to the point of injury<br /> <br /> Hypocrisy of the Champion (Heroes): Your target is completely incapable of questioning their motives, assuming that because their are right, their actions are justified, and vice versa","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T19:41:54-07:00","id":574652,"title":"","content":"I added Hunter, Demon and Mummy to my list of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=548527#post548527\"><b>cWoD Kinships</b></a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T22:46:10-07:00","id":577096,"title":"","content":"<b>It Watches You: </b>(Spirit)<br /> <b>Step 1: </b>Nature of the Fear (Everything around you is alive and judging you, <i>[The Shadow is Animistic]</i>)<br /> <b>Step 2:</b><ul><li>Normal Effect: Inflicts the Shadow Paranoia Condition.</li> <li>High Satiety: Also Inflicts the Spooked Condition.</li> <li>Satiety Expenditure: Compels the Target to repeat actions in a ritualistic manner to appease the spirits.</li> </ul><br /> <b>Step 3: </b>Manipulation (subtle dread) + Satiety vs Composure (provokes an immediate reaction) + Supernatural Tolerance<br /> <b>Step 4:</b> Ask the audience; is this too much?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T23:37:14-07:00","id":579528,"title":"","content":"This isn't Yours (Frankenstein Kinship): the victim becomes convinced their body parts don't really belong to them and have their own agendas. Satiety expenditure makes the latter point actually true.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T23:52:35-07:00","id":579536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=579528#post579528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This isn't Yours (Frankenstein Kinship): the victim becomes convinced their body parts don't really belong to them and have their own agendas. Satiety expenditure makes the latter point actually true.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dang it, I was thinking of posting something similar, based on Alien Hand Syndrome:<a href=\"http://syndrome.org/alien-hand-syndrome/\" target=\"_blank\">http://syndrome.org/alien-hand-syndrome/</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T00:24:23-07:00","id":579559,"title":"","content":"Hmmm... I'm considering something like &quot;You Can't Breath&quot; as a General Nightmare (or possibly Silent Geist Kinship, but it's pretty ubiquitous), playing off claustrophobia and particular suited to a Sphinx Beast (&quot;Sphinx&quot; literally meaning &quot;Strangler&quot;)... however, would it be best just to make that a particular way the damage-inducing fear of &quot;Behold, My True Form&quot; manifests?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T01:04:49-07:00","id":579597,"title":"","content":"Isn't it sad that you can't do Kinship with Unchained? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T01:51:13-07:00","id":579646,"title":"","content":"<b>Can Not Trust Yourself: </b>(Changeling/Fetch)<br /> <b>Step 1: </b>Nature of the Fear (Self Sabotage taken to extreme; your troubles are self inflicted, <i>[The Person in the Mirror Won't Let You Win]</i>)<br /> <b>Step 2:</b><ul><li>Normal Effect: Reduces the Threshold for the Exceptional Successes against the victim to 3, as the target subconsciously foils their own efforts.</li> <li>High Satiety: The victim treats a successful roll as though it only earned a single success.</li> <li>Satiety Expenditure: Also inflicts the False Memories (Persistent) Condition; the victim goes into denial and refuses to believe that anyone else is in any way responsible for their failures.</li> </ul><br /> <b>Step 3: </b>Wits (Self Doubt, sneaky, etc) + Satiety vs Resolve (erodes self-confidence) + Supernatural Tolerance<br /> <b>Step 4:</b> Ask the audience; is this too much?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T21:17:52-07:00","id":580523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jesuncolo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=579597#post579597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't it sad that you can't do Kinship with Unchained? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>In and of itself, yes - but I think a special case of something beyond the reach of kinship and the Beast's frame of reference provides a more valuable plot hook.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T23:27:46-07:00","id":580573,"title":"","content":"...I've posted three Nightmares and only just realized I haven't put anything for an Exceptional Success for any of them and have no idea where to start.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T06:40:37-07:00","id":580880,"title":"","content":"I can't think of a good nightmare, but I do have a house rule: a Nightmare doesn't work on the being who inspired it (I'm mostly thinking of the individual rather than which species or faction they belong to). It's a distillation of how <i>they're</i> scary, thus on some level the Nightmare's power is also their power, so it has no hold on them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T08:14:48-07:00","id":580963,"title":"","content":"As a good rule of thumb, okay, but I'd allow for exceptions.<br /> <br /> I mean yeah, a morbus isn't going to be afraid of disease, a spider host isn't likely to be afraid of spiders either, etc.<br /> <br /> But one of the more prominent fearmongers in fiction is obsessively terrified of the very thing he uses to terrify others. <br /> <br /> So just because say, someone else makes other people fear death doesn't mean they don't fear death too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T08:49:58-07:00","id":580984,"title":"","content":"Enemy At the Gates (Pure) - you can inflame the bigotries of a target, feeling vehemently threatened by whatever group they harbor suspicion of/contempt for. While this obviously has overtly evil uses to inflame prejudice driven persecution, it can also be used to do things like expose a bigot's true colors, teach them the foolishness of their ways, etc. Then again, since you have to have established Kinship with the Pure to learn the Nightmare, that says something about the Beast in and of itself...<br /> <br /> Break Your Mother's Back (Changeling) - instill a fear of violating silly superstitions in the target. With satiety expenditure you can actually tag them with condition to elicit dramatic failures for violating some bad-luck taboo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 07-06-2015, 04:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T10:06:37-07:00","id":581123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=580880#post580880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't think of a good nightmare, but I do have a house rule: a Nightmare doesn't work on the being who inspired it (I'm mostly thinking of the individual rather than which species or faction they belong to). It's a distillation of how <i>they're</i> scary, thus on some level the Nightmare's power is also their power, so it has no hold on them.</div> </div> </div> </div>You've never been afraid of yourself? Of what you could do? Ever took a step back to meditate on what you've done and how you'd have reacted if someone else did it on you? The butcher probably has nightmares about being hooked and chopped. Batman took this name because of the fear the bats invoked in him. Many people go crazy over the acts they've commited.<br /> <br /> Vampires fear vampirism more than anything because it would destroy their <i>soul. </i>Werewolves are trying to <i>control</i> the beast within and some fear the power of the Gauru. Mages have an integrity analog based on how <i>prudent</i> they are with their powers. Prometheans fear their very <i>existence</i> because of the Flux they generate. I think Nightmares should be usable against the one that inspired them. A bonus to resist might apply, but not immunity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T11:19:55-07:00","id":581248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=581123#post581123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You've never been afraid of yourself? Of what you could do? Ever took a step back to meditate on what you've done and how you'd have reacted if someone else did it on you?</div> </div> </div> </div>All the time, but it's not something other people are going to fear me over, which is what makes the basis for a Nightmare. Batman might be afraid of bats, but he can stand quite calmly amid a horde of them, and summon them to his aid, so it's not a fear that has a lot of power over him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T10:06:07-07:00","id":583559,"title":"","content":"I really wanted to make a beast with Mage Kinship, but neither of the Mage Nightmares were really doing it for me. Here's the one I came up with. It's kind of halfway between All Your Teeth Are Falling Out and Everything You Do Is Worthless.<br /> <br /> <b>You Don\u2019t Understand Anything</b> [Mage Kinship]<br /> <i>It turns out, all along, you\u2019ve misunderstood everything! All of your study, years of effort, is for naught! You know no more than the day you started.</i><br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Intelligence + Satiety vs. Resolve + Supernatural Tolerance<br /> <b>Normal: </b>The Beast chooses a Social or Mental Skill. The victim suddenly \u201crealizes\u201d that their understanding of that field is incorrect and find comprehending any information related to it difficult. The victim takes a -2 penalty to mundane applications of the chosen Skill.<br /> <b>High Satiety:</b> The victim is completely bewildered by the chosen Skill, as though all their training and knowledge were meaningless. Treat them as unskilled in that Skill (they lose all dots, Specialties, and take the unskilled penalty).<br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure: </b>As long as the Nightmare is active, the Beast may spend 1 Satiety to reduce the victim to a chance die on a single roll.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success: </b>Treat all of the victim\u2019s failures as dramatic failures.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","name":"MagicSwordsman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T12:44:37-07:00","id":583773,"title":"","content":"I have one more for the homebrew lines:<br /> <br /> <b>Eight Deadly Words (Dethroned Princess)</b><br /> The worst words a writer can hear from an audience is &quot;I Don't Care What Happens To These People&quot;. Like the most broken of Nobility, you understand what loss truly is, and you can tear away at the very ability of a person to care for others.<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Manipulation + Satiety vs. Resolve + Supernatural Tolerance<br /> <b>Normal:</b> The character ceases to care about others. New impressions made with them are poor, and they don't recover Willpower (or Wisps, for Nobility) when performing acts on other's behalf or interacting with friends, including the True Friend merit, even if it would fall under your Virtue to do so.<br /> <b>High Satiety:</b> The target temporarily becomes a high-functioning sociopath, unable to empathize with others (imposing a -3 penalty to Empathy and Animal Ken) and straining their relationships with others. Any time they would gain a beat from helping others, they instead gain a beat for acting in a self-centered manner.<br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> The target becomes utterly solipsistic, believing everyone else simply isn't a person. They may not make Empathy rolls of any kind, except to activate supernatural powers (such rolls lose the Empathy rating from their dice pool), and they are incapable of considering the emotions of others, nor the consequences of their actions on those around them. They lose their Virtue entirely and instead gain a second Vice: Selfish. Willpower gains from each vice are tracked separately, and so you can regain from both in the same scene.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T08:29:25-07:00","id":584767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MagicSwordsman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=583559#post583559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really wanted to make a beast with Mage Kinship, but neither of the Mage Nightmares were really doing it for me. Here's the one I came up with. It's kind of halfway between All Your Teeth Are Falling Out and Everything You Do Is Worthless.<br /> <br /> <b>You Don\u2019t Understand Anything</b> [Mage Kinship]<br /> <i>It turns out, all along, you\u2019ve misunderstood everything! All of your study, years of effort, is for naught! You know no more than the day you started.</i><br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Intelligence + Satiety vs. Resolve + Supernatural Tolerance<br /> <b>Normal: </b>The Beast chooses a Social or Mental Skill. The victim suddenly \u201crealizes\u201d that their understanding of that field is incorrect and find comprehending any information related to it difficult. The victim takes a -2 penalty to mundane applications of the chosen Skill.<br /> <b>High Satiety:</b> The victim is completely bewildered by the chosen Skill, as though all their training and knowledge were meaningless. Treat them as unskilled in that Skill (they lose all dots, Specialties, and take the unskilled penalty).<br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure: </b>As long as the Nightmare is active, the Beast may spend 1 Satiety to reduce the victim to a chance die on a single roll.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success: </b>Treat all of the victim\u2019s failures as dramatic failures.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;You know nothing, Jon Snow!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T22:01:17-07:00","id":613023,"title":"","content":"I like how plenty of these could work with others as well- The Consensus Is Wrong and You Don't Understand Anything could easily be Genius Kinships as well. <br /> <br /> Narrative Causality (Changeling or True Fae): Of course the butler did it. Of course the bomb only gets disarmed with one second left. Of course cars blow up when you shoot them. Of course stepmothers, foreigners, and people with mustaches are evil. At least, that's what the target thinks- this Nightmare forces the logic of fairytales and fiction onto the victim, making them assume that the most cliched answer must be the right one. <br /> <br /> Colorless Green Ideas Sleep Furiously (True Fae): The true horror of the Fae comes from how they can causally break the rules of reality and drag their victims off into bizarre realms where logic and physics are about as important as knock-knock jokes. This Nightmare attacks the victim's perception of reality, warping it so that up can be down, down can be purple, 1+1 can equal Uranus, and the floor is lava. <br /> <br /> Ludd Was Right (Genius, Clockstopper, any monster with a Luddite or technological bent): The target becomes fearful of modern technology and distrustful of science. <br /> <br /> Burden Of Proof (Banisher, Clockstopper): The target becomes aggressively skeptical, demanding massive amounts of proof for even the most vaguely out-of-the-ordinary occurrences. <br /> <br /> The Reptilian Agenda (Lemurian Mane): The target becomes fearful of reptiles and celebrities, believing that both are part of an alien conspiracy to rule the world from the shadows. <br /> <br /> The Fight Is Hopeless (Seer of the Throne): The target begins to fear that their enemies, and the supernatural forces behind the scenes in general, are much too vast and too powerful to be opposed, and they can only hope to be spared by bowing down and serving their superiors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T00:30:38-07:00","id":613073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jesuncolo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=579597#post579597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't it sad that you can't do Kinship with Unchained? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I must admit, I would have liked a &quot;God doesn't love you&quot; nightmare...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3648-nepher","name":"Nepher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3648_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-30T23:09:26-08:00","id":777564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=556347#post556347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just ideas I had, not sure what mechanics it would have;<br /> <br /> <b>Constraining Chains</b> (Ogre Changeling kinship)<br /> <i>You awaken somewhere, a dank dungeon, a basement with rust covered walls... It's hard to tell. You got to leave and realise you've been bound to the wall. Then 'It' comes and you know you have to get away... You tug at the bonds, but they don't break... They seem to get tougher... And at the same time, they're cutting into your flesh... It hurts but you need to get away... Until you realise the chains are slicing into your flesh and ripping through bone much worse than however 'That Thing' could do so...</i></div> </div> </div> </div><b>Constraining Chains</b> <b>(Ogre Changeling)</b><br /> <i>You awaken somewhere, a dank dungeon, a basement with rust covered walls. It's hard to tell. You try to leave and realise you've been bound to the wall. Then 'It' comes and you know you have to get away. You tug at the bonds, but they don't break. They seem to get tougher even as they\u2019re cutting into your flesh... It hurts but you need to get away, until you realise the chains are slicing into your flesh and ripping through bone much worse than however 'That Thing' could do so...</i><br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Presence + Satiety vs. Stamina + Supernatural Advantage<br /> <br /> <b>Normal:</b> None of us want to be tied up. Being bound leaves one vulnerable and without the liberty to fight back. The victim suffers the Immobilized Tilt as if his arms and legs are both bound for the scene. He rolls Strength + Athletics to break free at a -2 penalty.<br /> <br /> <b>High Satiety:</b> The victim suffers the Immobilized Tilt as if he were hogtied, inflicting a -4 penalty to all escape rolls.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> The victim\u2019s fear is so overpowering that he can barely concentrate enough to think clearly. In addition to the Immobilized Tilt, he suffers from the effects of the Insensate Tilt.<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success: </b>The phantom restraints placed on the victim seem to have a life of their own. Each attempt to break free only causes them to tighten further, injuring him further. In addition to the point of damage he suffers with every roll, the victim suffers additional damage equal to the number of failed dice in a Stamina roll.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> Not sure if this would even be a Kinship Nightmare for the Ogre Seeming, now that I look at it. It seems to make more sense if it were tied to a specific kith instead. Like the Brollachan. Or even the Leechfinger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":".  Changed the Resistance Attribute from Composure to Stamina. 01-28-2016, 11:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T03:36:10-08:00","id":777657,"title":"","content":"Can we get an admin to move this thread to the Beast Board?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T08:06:58-08:00","id":777766,"title":"","content":"<b>I'll Show You All! (Hoffnung Genius)</b><br /> <i>They mocked me, said my theories were nonsense. They had the nerve to call <b>me</b> mad!? But they'll see the truth soon enough.</i><br /> This Nightmare implants a delusion into the victim, one that they feel compelled to prove to others, even through violence.<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Manipulation + Satiety vs. Composure + Supernatural Advantage<br /> <br /> <b>Normal Effect: </b>The target gains a non-Persistent version of the Obsession Condition, tied to proving a specific delusion is true.<br /> <br /> <b>High Satiety: </b>The victim become dangerously fervent. Any time they fail to convince others, they suffer a Breaking Point.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure: </b>The target's mind has been thoroughly bent, permanently placing the delusion at the front of their mind. The Obsession Condition inflicted is Persistent.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T17:08:06-08:00","id":779369,"title":"","content":"First time I've written a Nightmare; hope I did alright. I'm not too aware of what is in the God-Machine Chronicles that differs from the previous version of World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> <b>Dem Bones Gonna Look All Over You</b> (Sin Eater, Boneyard power)<br /> Something overcomes you - the sense of being observed from an obscure angle by eyes that cannot be seen. Something is haunting you, you're sure. If only you could just see it.<br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool</b>: Presence + Satiety vs Composure + Supernatural Resistance<br /> <br /> <b>Normal</b>: The target becomes paranoid about being seen, whether they are within a building or not. They gain the Obsession condition to try and discover their observer, but are convinced to constantly look in the shadows, corners or in areas that people generally cannot fit. They feel a sensation that is akin to a when a Sin Eater enters an active Boneyard.<br /> <br /> <b>High Satiety</b>: The target hallucinates and sees reflections of someone indistinct watching them, or see someone out the corner of their eye, but they can never catch them within their vision.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure</b>: If the Beast remains within a mile of their target, they may project whispers into the target's ears, further disorientating them. This voice is distorted, though vaguely resembles their own voice.<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Succes</b>s: The target takes a penalty to their Investigation rolls equal to the Beast's successes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T21:43:14-08:00","id":786501,"title":"","content":"You Wet the Bed(Common)- The Beast causes the Victim to become filled with Embarrassment, Shame, and Disgust about themselves becoming grossed out and uncomfortable in their own skins.<br /> <br /> Worked out the concept but not the mechanics yet.<br /> <br /> First Post Back By the way, returning player that's been away since about 2009 shortly after Geist...Glad to be Back <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Keep your Friends Close and your Enemies at Knife point.","edited":{"userid":10265,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10265-neksys","user":"Neksys","date":". 12-15-2015, 01:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10265-neksys","name":"Neksys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10265_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T10:13:20-08:00","id":818549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares#post540642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because, surprisingly, there wasn't already a thread for this, even though Nightmares are literally designed to be homebrewed. Here until we get a Beast forum. Ideas or fully crunched mechanics are both fine, as are Nightmares based on homebrew templates.<br /> <br /> You Could Wake Up Dead Tomorrow (Sin-Eater): &quot;Oh Bart, don't worry, people die all the time. In fact, you could wake up dead tomorrow.&quot;. No idea what it would do, I just couldn't resist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Decided to try and flesh out this conceptual Nightmare.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b><u>\u200bAnything Could Kill You</u> (Forgotten Sin-Eater)</b><br /> <i>Don't worry, people die all the time. In fact, you could wake up dead tomorrow.</i><br /> <b>Dice Pool: </b>Manipulation + Satiety vs. Resolve + Supernatural Tolerance<br /> <br /> <b>Normal Effect</b>: The Beast can convince the target that a completely innocuous object, place, or situation is incredibly lethal. This inflicts the Paranoid Condition related to this compulsion for the remainder of the scene.<br /> <br /> <b>High Satiety:</b> A Sated Beast who uses this Nightmare can make the paranoia so overpowering that the victim succumbs to it. He inflicts the Resigned Condition.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> By expending a point of Satiety, the penalty levied by the Paranoid Condition is increased by half the Beast's Lair dots (rounded up).<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> The Nightmare also inflicts the Shadow Paranoia Condition","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 01-28-2016, 01:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T12:46:56-08:00","id":818650,"title":"","content":"Stay Out of My Head (Any supernatural prone to mind reading or mind control)<br /> <br /> Dice Pool: None, see below<br /> <br /> Action: Reflexive<br /> <br /> Normal: The Beast takes a -2 on his roll to invoke another Nightmare. In return he can &quot;store&quot; the Nightmare inside his mind for 24 hours. The next time someone uses a supernatural power to read or influence the Beast's mind that person is subjected to the Nightmare. The Beast may choose not to activate the Nightmare, if he is aware his mind is being accessed.<br /> <br /> High Satiety: The Beast may store a number of Nightmares up to his current Satiety. All Nightmares use the original roll. <br /> <br /> Satiety Expenditure: The invocation roll for the other Nightmare suffers no penalty and achieves an exceptional success at three successes instead of five.<br /> <br /> Exceptional Success: None, an exceptional success triggers the exceptional success result of the affected nightmare.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm also thinking how to make a Fetch based voodoo doll or Dorian Gray style nightmare. The horror trope of shared damage has pretty good precedent and would be cool to play with, I'm just thinking about how to make it effective without killing somebody outright<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T20:45:35-08:00","id":818966,"title":"","content":"Another Nightmare concept given mechanics.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Curiosity Killed the Cat</u> (Guardian of the Veil)<br /> Dice Pool:</b> Wits + Satiety vs. Resolve + Supernatural Advantage<br /> <br /> <b>Normal Effect:</b> The target becomes convinced that any attempt to investigate bizarre or supernatural occurrences is incredibly dangerous, and will obsessively avoid anything unusual. He gains the Obsession Condition related to this.<br /> <br /> <b>High Satiety:</b> The dangers perceived by all things bizarre and supernatural is so overpowering that it more often than not drives the target to flee. He gains the Frightened Condition to reflect this.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> The Conditions inflicted by the Nightmare become Persistent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T15:55:44-08:00","id":820021,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> <b><u>You Are One Of Them</u> (Frankenstein Promethean)<br /> Dice Pool:</b> Occult + Satiety vs. Resolve + Supernatural Advantage<br /> <br /> <i>You hate me because i'm a Monster? Look at yourself.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Normal Effect:</b> The Victim becomes convinced she is becoming an Promethean,she sees stiches growing between her fingers and joints,or her sking becomin infused with ectoplams<br /> <br /> <b>High Satiety:</b> The victim gets a taste of the Torment all created go through sooner or later, she starts to become more agressive and vengeful,she takes a 2 dice penalty on all not related to hurt someone over a slight.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> The Victim is afraid to leave her home,terryfied Disquiet may turn her loved ones against her,she gains thr agoraphobic condition","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T21:41:22-08:00","id":820147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=820021#post820021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b><u>You Are One Of Them</u> (Frankenstein Promethean)<br /> Dice Pool:</b> Occult + Satiety vs. Resolve + Supernatural Advantage<br /> <br /> <i>You hate me because i'm a Monster? Look at yourself.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Normal Effect:</b> The Victim becomes convinced she is becoming an Promethean,she sees stiches growing between her fingers and joints,or her sking becomin infused with ectoplams<br /> <br /> <b>High Satiety:</b> The victim gets a taste of the Torment all created go through sooner or later, she starts to become more agressive and vengeful,she takes a 2 dice penalty on all not related to hurt someone over a slight.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> The Victim is afraid to leave her home,terryfied Disquiet may turn her loved ones against her,she gains thr agoraphobic condition</div> </div> </div> </div> I think this could be re-phrased as Nightmare based on Prometheans in general. Normal Effect gives something like a self-imposed Shunned Condition and High Satiety gives something like a Berserk or Aggressive Condition. However, agoraphobia is kind of specific and too psychiatric of a term for a Condition, methinks. Maybe a Nomadic Condition that makes the target abandon their jobs and homes as if they were a Promethean trying to not create a Wasteland.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T06:01:32-08:00","id":820291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=820147#post820147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I think this could be re-phrased as Nightmare based on Prometheans in general. Normal Effect gives something like a self-imposed Shunned Condition and High Satiety gives something like a Berserk or Aggressive Condition. However, agoraphobia is kind of specific and too psychiatric of a term for a Condition, methinks. Maybe a Nomadic Condition that makes the target abandon their jobs and homes as if they were a Promethean trying to not create a Wasteland.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be rhemathically better,thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T12:09:00-08:00","id":828341,"title":"","content":"<u><b>You Cannot Warn Them</b></u><br /> <i>There are </i>things <i>out there in the dark. You can see them, crawling beyond the light. You need to tell everyone, warn them not to step into the shadows. But no matter what you try, no matter what you say, they don't understand. And you can only watch as they go beyond the light</i><br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool: </b>Manipulation + Satiety vs Resolve + Supernatural Advantage<br /> <br /> <b>Normal Effect:</b> The victim of this Nightmare finds it impossible to make himself understood by others. No matter what he says, his words are heard as gibberish, idiotic, irrelevant or irrational. This only applies to the spoken word however and does not effect writing. It will, however, effect sign language if the person uses that as their primary means of expression (if they are mute or deaf for example). Recording the person's words and them playing them back will not make them any clearer. The Nightmare attacks the victim's ability to communicate, not the abilities of those around him to comprehend.This effect lasts for a scene.<br /> <br /> <b>High Satiety: </b>Even the written word is corrupted by the Beast's power. The victim cannot use writing to communicate either, nor other secondary means of communication such as sign language or semaphore. This applies regardless of what the victim is using to record his words. No matter if the victim uses a computer, pencil and paper or carves his words into stone, they are equally unintelligible. This effect lasts for a scene but anything written or recorded during this period remains nonsense.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure: </b>Whatever the victim could not make others comprehend, he can no longer understand. The victim cannot decipher the speech (or if this is used at High Satiety, writings) of others. What is being said does not change, the victim simply cannot understand. This effect lasts for a scene.<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success: </b>The effects of the Nightmare last for a number of days equal to the Beast's Lair.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 10-16-2016, 01:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T12:27:33-08:00","id":828349,"title":"","content":"So. Any thoughts on it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T19:45:11-08:00","id":828563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=828349#post828349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So. Any thoughts on it?</div> </div> </div> </div>It looks pretty solid to me.<br /> <br /> Here's a somewhat-beneficial (for some given definition of beneficial) Nightmare:<br /> <br /> <b>Hide Your Love and Hate (Winter Court Changeling)</b><br /> <br /> <i>Know this: Emotion is weakness. Showing weakness is death. The moment any of these strangers know what you're really feeling, they'll have a thousand knives to twist in your heart. Make your heart like stone and nothing can touch you.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Wits + Satiety vs Resolve + Supernatural Tolerence<br /> <br /> <b>Normal Effect:</b> The victim finds displays of emotion deeply unsettling, be they her own or those of the people around her. For the rest of the scene, she must spend a point of Willpower to make any kind of social roll.<br /> <br /> <b>High Satiety:</b> The victim's heart hardens like an arctic glacier. Add the number of successes on this Nightmare to her total number of Doors. (If you aren't using Social Maneuvering rules, subtract the Beast's Lair from any social rolls made against the victim.)<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> The Beast swallows the victim's heart whole, guarding it against intruders. For the rest of the scene, any mundane social rolls made against the victim are automatically reduced to a chance die, and supernatural powers that would manipulate the victim's emotions invoke a Clash of Wills with the Beast.<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> The Nightmare lasts for 24 hours.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T07:03:18-08:00","id":828764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=828349#post828349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So. Any thoughts on it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dang. Imagine this being used alongside any of the Facets of my Shadow Gift of the Word.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T07:04:59-08:00","id":828766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=828563#post828563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It looks pretty solid to me.<br /> <br /> Here's a somewhat-beneficial (for some given definition of beneficial) Nightmare</div> </div> </div> </div>Somewhat beneficial, indeed.<br /> <br /> This basically is a good way of turning a warm, empathetic soul into his complete opposite.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> In other words, nicely done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T00:51:53-08:00","id":831569,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Made my first Nightmare. What do you think?<br /> <br /> <b>It's In Your Blood </b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u201c</span></span></span><i>There's nothing you can do to fight it. The abominable seeds planted generations ago are about to bloom. All the weaknesses and deviances of your ancestors are hiding in your own blood and calling for you. You're doomed to suffer their same fate as your own body and mind will betray you. Soon everyone will be able see it\u201d</i><br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool: </b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Intelligence + Satiety vs. Resolve + Supernatural Tolerance</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Normal: </b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">the victim gain the Paranoid Condition. She becomes convinced that there's some horrible secret or perversion that plagues her family which has tainted her very own genes. All those who can expose it or that are in the process of learning more about the past of her family and its members are seen as a threat.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>High Satiety: </b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">the victim gains the Broken Condition.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure: </b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">the victims enter a state of fugue. She attempts to flee the area and will violently attack anybody that tries to stop her even in the slightest. If that happens, she won't stop until her target is dead, at which point she regains her sense of self and won't remember much of the events, aside from a nightmarish recollection that has nothing to do with what really happened</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success: </b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">For the duration of the Nightmare, the victim suffers a -2 penalty on breaking point rolls</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 02-17-2016, 03:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T02:39:46-08:00","id":831618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=831569#post831569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Made my first Nightmare. What do you think?</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome work, as usual <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T07:00:24-08:00","id":831717,"title":"","content":"Here is a nightmare I made for a game I was running. The backstory behind this is my players are playing themselves from 4 years ago. At that time I (who happens to be the ST) am butchered by a rouge vampire. Turned into a puddle of red goo and meat jelly, along with everyone and everything in the house except for 1 person. My sister (the player who uses this nightmare) who witnesses this scene and is also witness to a vampire saving her life fighting against the other one.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">They are all dead</span></span><br /> In order to take this Nightmare a character has to have at least one close loved one slain by a supernatural being and be helpless to stop it.<br /> &quot;<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><i>Everyone you ever loved, ever cared about, ever held dear is dead laying at your feet. You couldn't stop it, you couldn't help, the lake of there blood is washing against you and your pathetic self. Can't you hear their cries still echoing in your head, as they beg for mercy, for god, for you, or anyone to help. Can't you feel their blood washing over you, as you stand there helpless.</i>&quot;</span><br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Manipulation + Satiety vs Resolve + Supernatural Tolerance<br /> <b>Normal:</b> The target cannot spend willpower to boost actions, as sorrow grips their heart and mind preventing them from putting their all into their actions.<br /> <b>High Satiety:</b> Target gains Depressed condition.<br /> <b>Spend Satiety: </b>Target views you as the only trustworthy being and a rock of salvation for one scene.<br /> <br /> <b>Depression</b><br /> you are depressed, more than sad your mind cannot find any form of joy any more. Your body aches and it takes effort just to roll out of bed and get food. You do simple things like work, eat, and crap because you aren't ready to die yet. The afflicted will only do the bear minium to survive, and must spend Willpower to do more.<br /> <b>Possible sources:</b> Supernatural powers, Life, Breaking Point<br /> <b>Resolution:</b> Seeking help<br /> <b>Beat:</b> Self Medicate- Gain a beat and the addicted condition to some intoxicant","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":600,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","user":"HaplessWithDice","date":". 02-17-2016, 11:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T18:41:42-08:00","id":832229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=828563#post828563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Hide Your Love and Hate (Winter Court Changeling)</b></div> </div> </div> </div>I can't help but think this should be called &quot;Conceal, Don't Feel.&quot; :P<br /> <br /> It's In Your Blood is certainly evocative, but... I'm not actually sure what the first level of it <i>does, </i>in game mechanics terms?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T14:31:20-07:00","id":854672,"title":"","content":"I have the problem of having a lot of ideas but not being great at working out mechanics. Here's an idea I had, sort of meant to fill a hole in terms of abilities that let Beasts deal with ghosts: some sort of &quot;ghost magnet&quot; nightmare gained from a Sin-Eater or necromancer that makes the victim a target for ghosts. I'm thinking the normal effect draws ghosts to them, the high satiety effect makes them more susceptible to numina, and the expenditure effect turns them into an anchor/binds a ghost to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T14:35:36-07:00","id":854675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=854672#post854672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have the problem of having a lot of ideas but not being great at working out mechanics. Here's an idea I had, sort of meant to fill a hole in terms of abilities that let Beasts deal with ghosts: some sort of &amp;quot;ghost magnet&amp;quot; nightmare gained from a Sin-Eater or necromancer that makes the victim a target for ghosts. I'm thinking the normal effect draws ghosts to them, the high satiety effect makes them more susceptible to numina, and the expenditure effect turns them into an anchor/binds a ghost to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>You Are Haunted?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T12:32:03-07:00","id":857242,"title":"","content":"Ah, another concept, one that I'm surprised I haven't seen or thought of before because it's such a classic &quot;monster&quot; power: a Nightmare that prevents or impedes the target from leaving a designated area. Doors close and lock themselves, people get lost and end up going back the way they came, space and geography change...for the name, maybe You Cannot Leave or No Exit (if you want to get away from the &quot;You&quot; formula).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T12:41:03-07:00","id":857249,"title":"","content":"Anyone come up with nightmares for Pangeans yet?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T20:02:59-07:00","id":858099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=857242#post857242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, another concept, one that I'm surprised I haven't seen or thought of before because it's such a classic &quot;monster&quot; power: a Nightmare that prevents or impedes the target from leaving a designated area. Doors close and lock themselves, people get lost and end up going back the way they came, space and geography change...for the name, maybe You Cannot Leave or No Exit (if you want to get away from the &quot;You&quot; formula).</div> </div> </div> </div>Kind of redundant isn't it? I mean sealed exits is already a lair trait. It is also doesn't really fit as a Nightmare as Nightmares are more anti-personal, but they don't really warp the world around the target.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T13:04:26-07:00","id":864472,"title":"","content":"<b>They Are Ready For You </b>(Hunter)<br /> <i>&quot;They know everything about you. They know how to hurt you, how to trick you, how to end you. You have no secrets from them, and you will end here if they so will it.&quot;</i><br /> <b>Dice Pool: </b>Wits+Satiety vs Manipulation + Supernatural Tolerance<br /> <b>Normal:</b> The Beast's player asks the target's player one question about the target's template or information on the target's character sheet, which must be answered truthfully with a yes or no.<br /> <b>High Satiety:</b> The Beast's player may instead ask up to (Composure) questions.<br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> The question(s) may be about anything involving the target. If the target's player does not know the answer, the Storyteller answers instead.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> <i>By forfeiting all questions to which she would be entitled, </i>the Beast may attempt to place an Anathema on the target as though she were a Hero, if and only if the target is a supernatural being. A Beast without the Sated Condition is immune as usual, as is a being with an Integrity-equivalent within its three-dot &quot;optimal&quot; range (that is, Clarity or Wisdom of 8, 9, or 10; Harmony of 4, 5, or 6, and so on). <i><span style=\"color:#008000\">[Mechanics for non-Beasts with Anathema to be inserted here.]</span></i><br /> <br /> <b>It Has Your Face</b> (Hunter)<br /> <i>&quot;You can easily justify destroying things that aren't like you. But what do you do when the monster is a human being? What do you do when you behead it - him - and see your own face looking back at you?&quot;</i><br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Manipulation+Satiety vs Composure+Supernatural Tolerance<br /> <b>Normal</b><b>:</b> The Beast gains an Integrity track, starting at (10-Satiety), and counts as both a mortal and a supernatural being for purposes of the target's breaking points.<br /> <b>High Satiety:</b> The Beast may make a cosmetic alteration to himself, as long as it makes him look more like the target.<br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> Any breaking points the target suffers involving the Beast are made at a -1 penalty, cumulative with all other penalties.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> Any damage or Tilts the Beast suffers are duplicated on the target.<br /> <br /> <b>You Don't Know The Rules </b>(Mortal)<br /> <i>&quot;The world doesn't make sense. The way it works keeps changing, and you can't figure out the pattern. It's almost maddening.&quot;</i><br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Intelligence+Satiety vs Intelligence+Supernatural Tolerance<br /> <b>Normal</b><b>:</b> The Beast creates a taboo, which the target must be physically and psychologically capable of keeping without danger or harm, which is told to the target's player. If the target breaks that taboo (target's Resolve*2) times, he may no longer apply Attributes to his defenses against supernatural powers. The Beast is also subject to the taboo, and must spend 1 Willpower each time to break it.<br /> <b>High Satiety:</b> The Beast is under no obligation to tell the target's player the taboo, but either her player or the Storyteller must tell the target's player when he breaks the taboo, and the target's player may ask a single question about the taboo with a yes-or-no answer. The Beast remains subject to the taboo.<br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> Unlike other Nightmares, a Beast may spend Satiety on this Nightmare during its duration as an instant action. The Beast changes the taboo once and resets the counter, as though she had invoked the Nightmare again at her current Satiety. Regardless of whether she has the High-Satiety effect, the target is aware that the rules have changed and enjoys a one-turn reprieve.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> Upon breaking the taboo the appropriate number of times, the target's unrolled defenses against supernatural powers are reduced to 0, and rolled defenses are reduced to a chance die.<br /> <br /> <b>They Just Keep Coming </b>(Mortal)<br /> <i>&quot;For every one of them you put down, two more take its place. You can't last forever, and you know that you will fall.&quot;</i><br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Resolve+Satiety vs Stamina+Supernatural Tolerance<br /> <b>Normal</b><b>:</b> If the target engages in Down and Dirty Combat, two successes are needed in place of one. Attacks made against the target still work normally.<br /> <b>High Satiety:</b> In addition to the normal effect, the target gains no bonuses from weapons.<br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> All damage the target inflicts has its type downgraded by one step.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> Any failure the target rolls on an attack is treated as a dramatic failure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making a fangame: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/867384-fangame-in-progress-xeno-the-beyond\" target=\"_blank\">Xeno: The Beyond</a>. A space alien game about identity, conformity, isolation, and colonialism. Please help!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10755-jy3ext","name":"jy3ext","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T13:29:51-07:00","id":864491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=858099#post858099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kind of redundant isn't it? I mean sealed exits is already a lair trait. It is also doesn't really fit as a Nightmare as Nightmares are more anti-personal, but they don't really warp the world around the target.</div> </div> </div> </div>It could work if it was all hallucinations. A common event in nightmares and horror movies is doors refusing to open and getting lost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/477-xenorath","name":"Xenorath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"169"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T06:23:43-07:00","id":865914,"title":"","content":"Anyone got ideas for a Nightmare centered around &quot;the cycle continuing itself&quot;, or the mechanics thereof?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T12:27:26-07:00","id":866487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=865914#post865914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone got ideas for a Nightmare centered around &quot;the cycle continuing itself&quot;, or the mechanics thereof?</div> </div> </div> </div>Which cycle?<br /> <br /> The Stars Are Right (Mummy, Leviathan): Target acts as though something that was Fated has come to pass.<br /> You Have Become What You Hate (Vampire, Hunter): Target begins transforming into a monster.<br /> You Can (Not) Advance (Changeling, Mummy): Target is unable to achieve any kind of personal growth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making a fangame: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/867384-fangame-in-progress-xeno-the-beyond\" target=\"_blank\">Xeno: The Beyond</a>. A space alien game about identity, conformity, isolation, and colonialism. Please help!","edited":{"userid":10755,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10755-jy3ext","user":"jy3ext","date":". 04-16-2016, 03:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10755-jy3ext","name":"jy3ext","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T11:47:16-07:00","id":894207,"title":"","content":"Idea prompt: <b>You Cannot Trust Your Eyes (Changeling/Sin-Eater with Phantasmal Key)</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T12:15:43-07:00","id":894228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jy3ext</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=866487#post866487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which cycle?<br /> <br /> The Stars Are Right (Mummy, Leviathan): Target acts as though something that was Fated has come to pass.<br /> You Have Become What You Hate (Vampire, Hunter): Target begins transforming into a monster.<br /> You Can (Not) Advance (Changeling, Mummy): Target is unable to achieve any kind of personal growth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doomed repetition of failure and/or action.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T11:06:08-07:00","id":917444,"title":"","content":"Aaand here I am, noticing that there are general Hunter Kinship's, but nothing specific. No Cheiron, no Lucifuge, no VASCU in the pool. Time to fix it, isn't it?<br /> <br /> <b>You're Just an Item: </b>(Cheiron Group Hunter, though I guess it could be repurposed for a Loyalist Changeling or a certain type of Deviant)<br /> <i>You've made the deal, you cashed in your boons, but now it's time for them to cash in theirs. They gave a clause. You won't do anything they don't want you to with what they gave you. And you'll do with it whatever they want you to. There is but a single problem. What they gave you, is you yourself. Your life. They own you. For them, you're nothing more than a mere tool like that screwdriver you're just holding. And if you won't serve, they'll break you, or make you serve by force. You wouldn't want it, right? Good. Now go, do as you're told.</i><br /> <b>Nature of the fear: </b>The fear that you're not belonging to yourself, that you don't have free will, are basically someone's slave and have to obey their every whim.<br /> <b>Normal effect: </b>When using the nightmare, choose a character, PC or NPC. The victim now belives it's entire life is owned by that character, and under threat of terrible consequences has to do as told. The victim gains a -2 penalty to acting against the chosen character until the end of the scene.<br /> <b>High Satiety: </b>The Victim subconsciously belives that his &quot;enslavement&quot; is fundamentally right and that his &quot;master's&quot; orders are the proper thing to do. Any action undertaken against the &quot;master&quot; removes the -2 penalty, but inspires the Guilty Condition on the victim until the end of the scene.<br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure: </b>The victim gains the Leveraged condition in regards to the chosen character. In addition, if the High Satiety effect of the Nightmare is active, the -2 penalty persists on all actions.<br /> <b>Dice Pool: </b>Wits+Satiety vs Resolve+Supernatural Tolerance<br /> <br /> <b>You Won't Repeat Their Mistakes: </b>(Lucifuge Hunter)<br /> <i>They screwed up, didn't they? Fathers, mothers, all those who fancy themselves as older and wiser, they've all been wrong all the time. They did the wrong thing. But you're not like them, are you? You'll do the right thing, and the right thing is certainly not what they say. </i><br /> <b>Nature of the fear: </b>Following in the footsteps of people who are or were morally wrong.<br /> <b>Normal Effect: </b>The victim has to spend a Willpower point to act in accordance with anyone in position of authority over him, beliving their decisions to be fundamentally wrong.<br /> <b>High Satiety: </b>Any rolls made while acting in accordance with anyone in position of authority over the victim suffers from a -2 penalty.<br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure: </b>Any roll made while acting in accordance with anyone in position of authrotiy over the victim suffers from a -3 penalty. This effect stacks with the High Satiety Effect.<br /> <b>Dice Pool: </b>Manipulation + Satiety vs Resolve + Supernatural Tolerance","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11117,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11117-inquisitor","user":"Inquisitor","date":". 09-22-2017, 05:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11117-inquisitor","name":"Inquisitor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T11:16:37-07:00","id":917454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Inquisitor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=917444#post917444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aaand here I am, noticing that there are general Hunter Kinship's, but nothing specific. No Cheiron, no Lucifuge, no VASCU in the pool. Time to fix it, isn't it?<br /> <br /> <b>You're Just an Item: </b>(Cheiron Group Hunter, though I guess it could be repurposed for a Loyalist Changeling or a certain type of Deviant)<br /> <i>You've made the deal, you cashed in your boons, but now it's time for them to cash in theirs. They gave a clause. You won't do anything they don't want you to with what they gave you. And you'll do with it whatever they want you to. There is but a single problem. What they gave you, is you yourself. Your life. They own you. For them, you're nothing more than a mere tool like that screwdriver you're just holding. And if you won't serve, they'll break you, or make you serve by force. You wouldn't want it, right? Good. Now go, do as you're told.</i><br /> <b>Nature of the fear: </b>The fear that you're not belonging to yourself, that you don't have free will, are basically someone's slave and have to obey their every whim.<br /> <b>Normal effect: </b>When using the nightmare, choose a character, PC or NPC. The victim now belives it's entire life is owned by that character, and under threat of terrible consequences has to do as told. The victim gains a -2 penalty to acting against the chosen character until the end of the scene.<br /> <b>High Satiety: </b>The Victim subconsciously belives that his &quot;enslavement&quot; is fundamentally right and that his &quot;master's&quot; orders are the proper thing to do. Any action undertaken against the &quot;master&quot; removes the -2 penalty, but inspires the Guilty Condition on the victim until the end of the scene.<br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure: </b>The victim gains the Leveraged condition in regards to the chosen character.<br /> <b>Dice Pool: </b>Wits+Satiety vs Resolve+Supernatural Tolerance<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This one is terrifying, arguably more so than You Can't Quit me or You Must obey. Good job! have a like!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T12:10:35-07:00","id":917483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=917454#post917454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This one is terrifying, arguably more so than You Can't Quit me or You Must obey. Good job! have a like!</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. I kinda-sorta imagine that using this one on a Changeling or a Demon(Especially the High Satiety effect) would cause the Freehold/Agency-thing-whatever to declare open war against you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11117-inquisitor","name":"Inquisitor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T12:19:28-07:00","id":917487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Inquisitor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=917483#post917483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah. I kinda-sorta imagine that using this one on a Changeling or a Demon(Especially the High Satiety effect) would cause the Freehold/Agency-thing-whatever to declare open war against you.</div> </div> </div> </div>I couldn't agree more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T05:48:29-07:00","id":917967,"title":"","content":"Continuing with conspiracy Kinship Nightmares:<br /> <b>They're Onto You: </b>(VASCU Kinship. Could be repurposed for Changeling, Deviant or a Magistos Mage)<br /> <i>They know it. They saw what you did, they hear what you're thinking, they know every your move, they're coming, and you can only run... No, scratch that. Even if you run, they find you. You can't do jack about them, only wait for them to come.</i><br /> <b>Nature of the fear: </b>Being stalked and chased by something that know more about you than you yourself and can see and predict your every move.<br /> <b>Normal Effect: </b>The victim believes that some unknown beings are constantly spying on it trying to punish it for some unspecified atrocities. The victim gains the Paranoid condition.<br /> <b>High Satiety: </b>The victim's fear of being surveiled and captured leads it to panic at the very thought of whatever migh the beings do to him unless he somehow escapes their grasp. The victim suffers a -2 penalty to all actions not involving running from the ones he believes to be after her.<br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure: </b>The victim thinks that the atrocity he's being chased for actually happens and is able to recall it in great detail. In addition, he belives that those surveiling him have all the right to do so for said crime. He gains the Guilty condition<br /> <b>Dice Pool: </b>Manipulation + Satiety vs Composure + Supernatural Tolerance<br /> <br /> <b>You're Impure: </b>(Malleus Maleficarum Kinship.)<br /> <i>You've sinned. You've sinned greatly, and as any other sinner before you, you will go to Hell. And you know what awaits those who end up in Hell? That's right. Suffering. You do not want to suffer, do you? But there is still a chance for your soul. Go, my child, and do good in the name of the lord.</i><br /> <b>Nature of the Fear: </b>Fear of being punished for one's misdeeds.<br /> <b>Normal Effect: </b>The victim believes that he's commited misdeeds that he will be punished for, in Hell, by Karma, appropriately to beliefs, and that the only way to avert that is by comitting good deeds. Any time the victim is presented with an opportunity to fulfill his virtue during the scene he must roll a reflexive Resolve + Composure check to resist doing so.<br /> <b>High Satiety: </b>The victim now can no longer regain willpower from fulfilling his vice. Instead, he loses willpower by doing so.<br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure: </b>The victim can't regain willpower by any other means than fulfilling his or her virtue or vice (Or only virtue, if the High Satiety effect applies.). In addition, fulfilling the virtue now only provides one point of Willpower.<br /> <b>Dice Pool: </b>Wits+Satiety vs Resolve+Supernatural Tolerance<br /> <br /> Both are pretty straightforwards and flavorwise uncreative, but I still consider them somehow interesting.<br /> Lemme know what other Conspiracies would you like to see next.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11117-inquisitor","name":"Inquisitor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T05:52:00-07:00","id":917968,"title":"","content":"If Demons were available for Kinship, They're Onto You would be perfect for them. Personally I houserule it so that is possible, as I see little reason why they can't, but that's just me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T06:25:50-07:00","id":917988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=917968#post917968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Demons were available for Kinship, They're Onto You would be perfect for them. Personally I houserule it so that is possible, as I see little reason why they can't, but that's just me.</div> </div> </div> </div>If we were accepting GM stuff for Kinships, I'd think that They're Onto You would fit more with Angels than Demons, but that's just my personal opinion. Overall, It is actually a pretty flexible one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11117-inquisitor","name":"Inquisitor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T06:30:10-07:00","id":917990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Inquisitor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=917988#post917988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we were accepting GM stuff for Kinships, I'd think that They're Onto You would fit more with Angels than Demons, but that's just my personal opinion. Overall, It is actually a pretty flexible one.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it would work pretty well for both. Angels certainly have that vibe to them, as do demons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T05:33:38-07:00","id":934419,"title":"","content":"I've written an ivory claw kinship for a game I'm currently playing<br /> <br /> <b>You're Not Good Enough </b>(Ivory Claw Kinship)<br /> <i>You're worthless, you know it. They can all tell, you might as well just give up and stop trying. No matter how hard you try you're just going to fail.</i><br /> <br /> Dice Pool: wits + satiety vs resolve + supernatural tolerance<br /> Normal Effect: The target suffers the broken condition.<br /> High Satiety Effect: 8-again on social rolls made against the target<br /> Satiety Expenditure Effect: The broken condition becomes persistent<br /> Exceptional success: The target suffers a -1 to all actions taken (-2 if the high effect is also used)<br /> <br /> I've also toyed with the idea of making the high satiety effect cause a -4 to all actions within a specific category (like the <b>Everything You Do Is Worthless </b>normal effect).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6365,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","user":"Fumus","date":".  Forgot dice pool 07-21-2016, 04:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T13:59:12-07:00","id":939118,"title":"","content":"<b>Unhallowed Ground (SinEater w/ Boneyard) - (Modeled after You Are Infected)</b><br /> <i>&quot;Hey, did you hear that? What do you mean no? This place is creepy man, I swear. I have to get out of here.&quot;</i><br /> <b>Normal</b>: The Beast infuses an area with a nightmare for one scene. The area must be contiguous and have some distinct designation ex The clearing at the center of forest street, the hotel lobby, Turner Graveyard. The next individual to enter the area who is not the Beast or a member of her Brood triggers the nightmare to be rolled at -2. Any decisions for the nightmare must be made at the time it is infused in the area rather than when it is rolled. The Beast does not know who triggered the Nightmare but does know when it was triggered.<br /> <b>High Satiety</b>: As above but the Beast takes a -4 roll to invoke a nightmare and suffuses a location with it's essence. Anyone who enters the location suffers its effects while they remain there. <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure</b>: The combined Nightmare lasts for a full day.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success</b>: The Beast receives an instinctual impression of the target. While they do not specifically see him, they could describe standout features such as male, tall, scarred. If the Beast encounters the individual they can roll Intelligence + Resolve + 2 to identify them as someone who was effected by their nightmare.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10415-vermillionde","name":"VermillionDe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T09:51:36-07:00","id":939595,"title":"","content":"<b>Tainted Waters (Obrimos Mage or Ordo Dracul Vampire)</b><br /> <i>&quot;I knew the resonance of that Hallow was strong, but nothing like this... There's this buzzing in my ear now, it's almost like I can hear whispers. I think they're getting louder,..&quot;</i><br /> <b>Normal:</b> The Beast uses the Hallow, Node, Wyrm's Next or other Font of magical energy to infect the last individual to pull energy from that location with a nightmare. The Beast rolls at -2 in order to affect them.<br /> <b>High Satiety:</b> The Beast infuses a Font of magical energy with a nightmare. The Beast rolls for the nightmare at -4 and the next time any entity pulls energy from that location they immediately suffer its effects.<br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> For each Satiety spent the Beast can infect an additional target that takes from the source of energy.<br /> Exceptional Success: As per activated Nightmare.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10415-vermillionde","name":"VermillionDe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T01:09:33-07:00","id":968406,"title":"","content":"<b>Your Life Is Mine (Leechfinger Changeling)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool: </b>Presence + Satiety \u2013 Stamina<br /> <br /> <b>Normal: </b>The attack inflicts one point of lethal damage per success. Victims who die from this Nightmare\u2019s effects are found drained of something vital: blood, breath, water, or even their youth.<br /> <br /> <b>High Satiety: </b>The attack drains points of supernatural resources (Vitae, Essence, Mana, etc) or Willpower for targets who do not have such resources, equal to the Beast\u2019s Lair dots.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> For the duration of the scene, each point of damage caused by this Nightmare will heal one point of bashing damage suffered by the Beast or downgrade one point of her lethal damage to bashing damage.<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success: </b>A successful attack counts as fulfilling the Beast\u2019s Hunger (based Satiety potential of 3)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T01:59:57-07:00","id":968418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=968406#post968406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Your Life Is Mine (Leechfinger Changeling)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool: </b>Presence + Satiety \u2013 Stamina<br /> <br /> <b>Normal: </b>The attack inflicts one point of lethal damage per success. Victims who die from this Nightmare\u2019s effects are found drained of something vital: blood, breath, water, or even their youth.<br /> <br /> <b>High Satiety: </b>The attack drains points of supernatural resources (Vitae, Essence, Mana, etc) or Willpower for targets who do not have such resources, equal to the Beast\u2019s Lair dots.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> For the duration of the scene, each point of damage caused by this Nightmare will heal one point of bashing damage suffered by the Beast or downgrade one point of her lethal damage to bashing damage.<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success: </b>A successful attack counts as fulfilling the Beast\u2019s Hunger (based Satiety potential of 3)</div> </div> </div> </div>This is really cool, although does that High Satiety version drain fuel in addition to health or instead of it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T02:17:10-07:00","id":968423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=968418#post968418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is really cool, although does that High Satiety version drain fuel in addition to health or instead of it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! The resource drain is in addition to the health damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T02:22:12-07:00","id":968424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=968406#post968406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Your Life Is Mine (Leechfinger Changeling)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool: </b>Presence + Satiety \u2013 Stamina<br /> <br /> <b>Normal: </b>The attack inflicts one point of lethal damage per success. Victims who die from this Nightmare\u2019s effects are found drained of something vital: blood, breath, water, or even their youth.<br /> <br /> <b>High Satiety: </b>The attack drains points of supernatural resources (Vitae, Essence, Mana, etc) or Willpower for targets who do not have such resources, equal to the Beast\u2019s Lair dots.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> For the duration of the scene, each point of damage caused by this Nightmare will heal one point of bashing damage suffered by the Beast or downgrade one point of her lethal damage to bashing damage.<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success: </b>A successful attack counts as fulfilling the Beast\u2019s Hunger (based Satiety potential of 3)</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that Exceptional Success effect is really appropriate to be honest. How does a Makara that collects ships to store in her Lair get Satiety from drinking someone's life essence?<br /> Nightmares probably shouldn't have any way to restore Satiety period, it interacts really weirdly with the current system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T02:27:17-07:00","id":968425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=968424#post968424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think that Exceptional Success effect is really appropriate to be honest. How does a Makara that collects ships to store in her Lair get Satiety from drinking someone's life essence?<br /> Nightmares probably shouldn't have any way to restore Satiety period, it interacts really weirdly with the current system.</div> </div> </div> </div>Several canon Nigtmares have this option, it's not new. Look at 'You Are Better Than Them'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T02:32:27-07:00","id":968427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=968425#post968425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Several canon Nigtmares have this option, it's not new. Look at 'You Are Better Than Them'.</div> </div> </div> </div>It still doesn't seem like a great idea even for the canon ones, but then again, I'm not a game designer.<br /> The Nightmare itself does absolutely seem appropriate for that Kinship, though!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T02:37:05-07:00","id":968429,"title":"","content":"Thank you!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T18:31:04-08:00","id":1017428,"title":"","content":"<b>Your Shape Is Not Your Own</b> [Idigam Kinship]<br /> <br /> <b>Dicepool</b>: Manipulation + Satiety vs Resistance + Rank<br /> <br /> <b>Normal Satiety:</b> The Beast gains the ability to perceive and interact with ghosts and spirits in Twilight. If he can already do this through another power, add +1 to his dice pool. When targeting these entities, he may imitate the Ghost Manipulation or Spirit Manipulation powers of the Idigam, replacing Rank with Lair.<br /> <br /> <b>High Satiety:</b> The Beast can impose the nature of his Horror on a spirit or ghost, rather than only shifting around their pre-existing traits. The ghost or spirit gains a number of Numina, Influence dots and/or Dread Power dots equal to the Beast\u2019s Lair. These must reflect powers the Beast possesses.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> The Beast can force a ghost or spirit to merge with a living being for a scene. The resulting hybrid is a pseudo-Claimed with the ephemeral\u2019s Essence pool and all of its Influences, Numina and Dread Powers. For its other traits, use the Brief Nightmare rules with the ephemeral\u2019s Rank as a guideline.<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success: </b>The changes caused by this Nightmare last for a number of days equal to Lair rather than a scene.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T23:55:59-08:00","id":1018364,"title":"","content":"<b><u>You Made a Deal (Changeling Kinship)</u></b><br /> <br /> <i>You made that bargain, and now it hangs around your neck like a chain. You know what will happen if you try to break your word. You know how you'll suffer.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Dicepool: </b>Manipulation + Satiety vs Resolve + Supernatural Tolerance<br /> <br /> <b>Normal Satiety:</b> This Nightmare can only be activated immediately after the intended victim has made a promise, deal or vow, although it need not be with the Beast himself. When activating this Nightmare, activate another simultaneously. The second Nightmare will hang over the victim's head like the proverbial Sword of Damocles for (Lair + Satiety) days, taking effect if the victim attempts to go against the letter of his word. The Nightmare will only take effect the first time the victim tries to transgress against the bargain.<br /> <br /> <b>High Satiety: </b>The Beast is automatically made awarewhen the victim tries to break his word.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure: </b>For every dot of Satiety spent, the Nightmare 'attached' to this one gains another 'charge', meaning that if three dots are expended, the Nightmare will take effect the first, second, third and fourth times that the victim attempts to break his word.<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success: </b>On an Exceptional Success, the victim must roll Resolve + Composure to attempt to transgress against the bargain, as he gains a bone-deep certainty that if he does so, he will suffer some horrific retribution.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T21:06:12-08:00","id":1020164,"title":"","content":"I've got some. Haven't thought up the mechanics on them, though.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>I Must Scream:</b> A nightmare that suppresses or even completely nullifies sound in the area, preventing the Beast's prey from calling for help.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Tiny Terror:</b> Instilling the victim with crippling self doubt, even a low level threat can send the Beast's prey cowering in fear.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Drop Dead:</b> An overpowering surge of terror renders the victim unconscious if they fail to resist its effects.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Double Dream:</b> The Beast generates not one, but two illusionary environments that occur in succession with each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T01:49:46-08:00","id":1050370,"title":"","content":"<u><b>You must have it</b></u><br /> <b>Roll</b>: Intelligence + Satiety vs. Composure + Supernatural Tolerance<br /> <b>Effect</b>: This certain item is all that matters. Possessing it is life, not having it is death. The victim becomes obsessed with an item of the Beast's choice for a scene, acquiring it the only thing on its mind. Once in his or her possession, the condition is resolved.<br /> <b>High Satiety effect</b>: Acquiring the item does not resolve the condition; rather, the victim jealously defends his possession until the end of the scene.<br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure</b>: Rather than for a scene, the victim is obsessed with the item for 24 hours.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success</b>: Violent actions towards acquiring the items enjoy a +2 Bonus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T12:12:12-08:00","id":1058109,"title":"","content":"I'm trying to create a less lethal version of Behold My True Form that could be reliably used to terrify people without accidently putting them in the hospital on a good roll. Any advice on that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T14:42:06-08:00","id":1058152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=1058109#post1058109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm trying to create a less lethal version of Behold My True Form that could be reliably used to terrify people without accidently putting them in the hospital on a good roll. Any advice on that?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not really. I mean, you might try to flavor <b>Run Away</b>, or <b>Fear is Contagious</b> so that you show off what you really are and make them flee. If you're an Incarnate, it's even worse, because showing your face can turn people to stone. That's all it says, doesn't give any mechanics for it. Just: they look at you, and boom, they're petrified!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T15:50:52-08:00","id":1058182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=1058152#post1058152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Not really. I mean, you might try to flavor <b>Run Away</b>, or <b>Fear is Contagious</b> so that you show off what you really are and make them flee. If you're an Incarnate, it's even worse, because showing your face can turn people to stone. That's all it says, doesn't give any mechanics for it. Just: they look at you, and boom, they're petrified!</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking of Run Away, what happens if the victim(s) are physically unable to run away for the entire duration of the Nightmare? Perhaps give them some sort of COndition?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T12:55:13-08:00","id":1058525,"title":"","content":"What about a nightmare that gave the victim a different personality ala Dissociative Identity Disorder?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T13:04:00-08:00","id":1058530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=1058525#post1058525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about a nightmare that gave the victim a different personality ala Dissociative Identity Disorder?</div> </div> </div> </div>You Are Not Alone In Your Head? You Are Mad (ala Macbeth)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T14:16:21-08:00","id":1058566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=1058530#post1058530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You Are Not Alone In Your Head? You Are Mad (ala Macbeth)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Could work. What if you wanted them to believe they were someone specific? Or even implant your own mind onto theirs? Like that one VtM Domination power?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T16:45:21-08:00","id":1058652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=1058566#post1058566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could work. What if you wanted them to believe they were someone specific? Or even implant your own mind onto theirs? Like that one VtM Domination power?</div> </div> </div> </div>* In Your Head<br /> * You Are Me<br /> * You Are Not Yourself<br /> * You Are Someone Else","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T18:22:20-08:00","id":1058722,"title":"","content":"Definitely Changeling Kinship Nightmares","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T05:50:38-08:00","id":1058925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=1058722#post1058722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Definitely Changeling Kinship Nightmares</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Speaking of Which...<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Frog's Kiss:</b> Not all monsters are cursed to be forever alone. Many legends involve such creatures being able to cast off their hideous visages in exchange for being shown an act of compassion or love from humanity. With this Nightmare, the Beast can make themselves appear more charming towards others and convince them to lend aid to the monster. But just like the story of a princess kissing a frog, such compliance may not be socially acceptable in the eyes of others.<br /> <br /> Mechanics aren't planned out, but I'm thinking it would help the Beast during <b>persuasion</b> and <b>seduction</b> attempts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 03-06-2017, 08:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T06:01:27-08:00","id":1058932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=1058925#post1058925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of Which...<br /> <br /> <b>Frog's Kiss:</b> Not all monsters are cursed to be forever alone. Many legends involve such creatures being able to cast off their hideous visages in exchange for being shown an act of compassion or love from humanity. With this Nightmare, the Beast can make themselves appear more charming towards others and convince them to go along with their schemes. But just like the story of a princess kissing a frog, such compliance may not be socially acceptable around others.<br /> <br /> Mechanics aren't planned out, but I'm thinking it would help the Beast during <b>persuasion</b> and <b>seduction</b> attempts.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Alien Allure Atavism kind of covers that. That said, an alternative Nightmare could work.<br /> <br /> For effects, perhaps it's something which involves the Charmed and/or Swooning Condition? Also, here's some flavor text to go with that.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <i>You'd do anything for her. You know you shouldn't, but how could you bring yourself to possibly deny her?</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T10:07:55-08:00","id":1059054,"title":"","content":"RE: Frog's Kiss<br /> I agree that alien allure Covers that... Unless you can Designate Someone Else As the Object Of infatuation, effectively playing evil Amor. Such passion, especially if you are in a happy relationship atm, and Suddenly developed intense feelings for someone (or someTHING) else would be a nightmarish experience. Bonus points if it's a mix of disgust and love- in the original fairy tale, the Princess threw the froh against a wall rather than Kiss him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T09:07:59-08:00","id":1059557,"title":"","content":"Ooh ooh! What about an Acanthus Kinship Nightmare that makes the victim think they're trapped in a loop? Doomed to repeat the same sequence of events until they surrender completely to their fate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T13:16:48-08:00","id":1059709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=1059557#post1059557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ooh ooh! What about an Acanthus Kinship Nightmare that makes the victim think they're trapped in a loop? Doomed to repeat the same sequence of events until they surrender completely to their fate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Groundhog Day as a Nightmare? I love it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T14:22:36-08:00","id":1059748,"title":"","content":"Another idea for an Acanthus, Arisen or possibly Changeling Kinship: It Is Written. Causes the victim to believe that something is fated/certain to come to pass, and thus does nothing to resist it. The Nightmare creates a self-fulfilling prophecy, so to speak.<br /> <br /> I guess that might be better handled as a reskinning of You Must Obey, though. Meh. Whatever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T00:22:37-08:00","id":1059974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=1059748#post1059748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another idea for an Acanthus, Arisen or possibly Changeling Kinship: It Is Written. Causes the victim to believe that something is fated/certain to come to pass, and thus does nothing to resist it. The Nightmare creates a self-fulfilling prophecy, so to speak.<br /> <br /> I guess that might be better handled as a reskinning of You Must Obey, though. Meh. Whatever.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree that it's just a reskinning of You must Obey.<br /> The fear of something going to happen and being unable to do anything against it, perhaps even ending up helping it along?<br /> Something like this maybe:<br /> <br /> <u><b>It is Written </b></u>(Arisen/Changeling/Acanthus Kinship)<br /> <i>There is nothing you can do: it will happen. It has to. It is destiny. </i><br /> <b>Roll</b>: Intelligence + Satiety vs. Composure + Supernatural Tolerance<br /> <b>Effect</b>: The Beast decides on a certain development: you will break up with your girlfriend, your wife will find out about your affair, you will get fired, you will get the promotion you don't want to get because it would mean you will have to move to the other side of the continent.... For the next 24 hours, the victim is unable to stop it: the victim gains the Delusional Condition, and cannot spend Willpower. Rolls to go against his 'fate' do not have the 10-again quality, rolls to give in and pursue his fate gain the 9-again quality.<br /> <b>High Satiety effect</b>: Bit by bit, the victim gives in: in addition to the normal effect, any failed roll is treated as a dramatic failure AND the victim loses a point of willpower for the enourmous effort it takes to go against fate should he roll a success.<br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure</b>: Despite his wishes, the victim appears like he is really intent on achieving the development: he gains a penalty to acting against his fate that is equal to the Beast's Lair. Should he give in and try to fulfill his fate, this will become a bonus. In addition, any roll that is not an exceptional success is treated as a failed roll, as his denying wanting the promotion is seen as humbleness, and his denying of having an affair comes across as a really lame lie.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success</b>: Rolls that give in to his fate enjoy the 8-again quality, and the effect lasts 48 hours instead of 24.<br /> <br /> <br /> This nighmare can be stopped early by resolving the Delusional Condition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T00:45:27-08:00","id":1059982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=1059974#post1059974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I disagree that it's just a reskinning of You must Obey.<br /> The fear of something going to happen and being unable to do anything against it, perhaps even ending up helping it along?<br /> Something like this maybe:<br /> <br /> <u><b>It is Written </b></u>(Arisen/Changeling/Acanthus Kinship)<br /> <i>There is nothing you can do: it will happen. It has to. It is destiny. </i><br /> <b>Roll</b>: Intelligence + Satiety vs. Composure + Supernatural Tolerance<br /> <b>Effect</b>: The Beast decides on a certain development: you will break up with your girlfriend, your wife will find out about your affair, you will get fired, you will get the promotion you don't want to get because it would mean you will have to move to the other side of the continent.... For the next 24 hours, the victim is unable to stop it: the victim gains the Delusional Condition, and cannot spend Willpower. Rolls to go against his 'fate' do not have the 10-again quality, rolls to give in and pursue his fate gain the 9-again quality.<br /> <b>High Satiety effect</b>: Bit by bit, the victim gives in: in addition to the normal effect, any failed roll is treated as a dramatic failure AND the victim loses a point of willpower for the enourmous effort it takes to go against fate should he roll a success.<br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure</b>: Despite his wishes, the victim appears like he is really intent on achieving the development: he gains a penalty to acting against his fate that is equal to the Beast's Lair. Should he give in and try to fulfill his fate, this will become a bonus. In addition, any roll that is not an exceptional success is treated as a failed roll, as his denying wanting the promotion is seen as humbleness, and his denying of having an affair comes across as a really lame lie.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success</b>: Rolls that give in to his fate enjoy the 8-again quality, and the effect lasts 48 hours instead of 24.<br /> <br /> <br /> This nighmare can be stopped early by resolving the Delusional Condition.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the way that this Nightmare could be used both to help an ally, or against an enemy. Wouldn't be nice for either of them, but a 'glorious fate' would be an interesting one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T04:27:20-08:00","id":1060024,"title":"","content":"Thanks. Needs some balancing though - the stacking of the high satiety effect and the satiety expenditure would be overpowered. Maybe instead of making any non-exceptional succes a failure, it should detract 2 Successes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T05:30:43-08:00","id":1060032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=1060024#post1060024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks. Needs some balancing though - the stacking of the high satiety effect and the satiety expenditure would be overpowered. Maybe instead of making any non-exceptional succes a failure, it should detract 2 Successes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps we could just explicitly state that those effects do not stack?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T01:22:50-07:00","id":1066735,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar10397_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10397\" data-vbnamecard=\"10397\">ajf115</a> That could work.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u><b>You don't matter:</b></u><br /> Intelligence + Satiety vs. Resolve + Supernatural Resistance<br /> <i>Nothing you do has meaning. Why even try? Why not just stop struggling at all? Just lay down and wait for death...</i><br /> <b>Normal</b>: The victim gains the Lethargic condition, and loses access to his specialties as well as the 10-again quality. Those would mean that they are somehow special and can contribute, after all.<br /> <b>High Satiety</b>: <i>You have no impact. </i>When participating in a team effort, expectional successes yield one success. Normal successes are treated as failures. In addition, the target cannot fall asleep for the duration of the Nightmare.<br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure</b>: The victim's Resolve is considered to be 1 for the duration of the Nightmare. In addition, since the victim is preoccupied with pondering the meaninglessness of their efforts, Wits-related rolls are penalized by the Beast's Lair.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success</b>: The Nightmare lasts 24 hours<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T15:00:58-07:00","id":1070870,"title":"","content":"You Are Wrong: A Nightmare that makes it impossible to relay a fact/prove something to others. Testimony is dismissed out of hand. Evidence goes missing in a hundred silly little ways or else becomes obviously false. Eventually, even you come to doubt whether or not you just made a mistake.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T19:55:45-07:00","id":1070997,"title":"","content":"Because the kinship <i>might</i> happen...<br /> <br /> <b>You Are Filler (Hero Kinship)</b><br /> <i>Did you think you were the hero of this story? You're not. You're not even the villain. You're just the spear-carrier, the mook, the faceless extra in the background. Now shut up and let the stars play their roles. There is no room in this tale for a nobody like you.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Roll</b>- Intelligence + Satiety vs Resolve + Supernatural Resistance<br /> <br /> <b>Normal Effect</b>- the victim understands that they are not the main character in the story of their life, and they act according. For as long as this nightmare affects them, they must make a reflexive Resolve+Presence roll (and beat the beast's successes) to do anything that would draw significant attention to them (attack someone, make a speech, destroy something, etc)<br /> <br /> <b>High Satiety- </b>The victim knows their role is to respond, not to act. They need to make the reflexive roll to initiate things that draw even minor attention to themselves. Starting a conversation. crying for help, pointing out the intruder- all of these are for the major players, not them.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure</b> - The mook's role has always been to die for the hero. Record the number of successes that the Beast rolls. For as long as the nightmare continues, if the beast is damaged they can trade the a success to transfer a point of damage to someone affected by the nightmare. By distortions in perception, the attack hits the extra instead. They cannot use any defenses, mundane or magical, against this- however, if they survive, they are instantly freed from the nightmare.<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success </b>- The reflexive roll has a -2 penalty.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>You Are Just An Animal (Insatiable Kinship)</b><br /> <i>Look at you hairless monkeys. You think you are the rulers of this world, the pinnacle of evolution. But the sea and the sky, the earth and flame and void, they know the truth. There were &quot;pinnacles of evolution&quot; before you, and there will be after you. For all your arrogance, ape, you're nothing more then another species of prey.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Roll- </b>Intelligence+ Satiety vs Composure + Supernatural Resistance<br /> <br /> <b>Normal Effect- </b>The Illusion that is civilisation fades away from the victim, as they start slipping back into the primitive thought patterns of the first hominids (or at least, what we think the first hominids were like). Any actions that would require concepts more complex then a smart animal could grasp take a -2 penalty*<br /> <br /> <b>High Satiety- </b>Humanity relies so much on their machines. Yet another sign of their hubris. For as long as the nightmare lasts, any machine created less then (10 x number of success) years ago simply doesn't work for the victim. No matter how hard they try, it simply doesn't respond to their instructions.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure - </b>Humans were once just another beast in the field. They will be again. A single human victim immediately reverts down to the state of a wild animal. Their intelligence drops down to 0, and they are incapable of using language or performing any action penalised by the normal effect.<br /> In addition, the beast can give the victim one instinct that they will attempt to act out to the best of their ability. This can be any behaviour seen in the animal kingdom. It doesn't necessarily have to be an animal related to humanity, but it does have to be an instinct the victim could biologically fulfil.<br /> This power lasts for the rest of the scene- once it is reversed, the victim only has vague and fragmented memories of what happened. Unless they see evidence, the memories quickly fade.<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success- </b>The victim also loses 10-again on penalised roles<b>.</b><br /> <br /> *(Note that animals aren't stupid- dolphins can grasp basic maths, apes can comprehend melee weapons and virtually all social animals can manipulate or deceive. This penalty applies mostly to actions like complex technology, academia, politics, crafting and otherwise clearly &quot;human&quot; actions)<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, a helpful nightmare!<br /> <br /> <b>You Are Feared (Common)</b><br /> <i>Look at you. Beaten down, cowering, fleeing from monsters on all sides. Don't you wish you knew what it was like to be the powerful one, to be the terrible thing that the weak quiver and weep at the sight of?<br /> Here. Let it never be said monsters cannot be kind.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Roll</b>- As base nightmare (see below)<br /> <br /> <b>Normal Effect</b>- The beast uses another nightmare on the target, with a -2 penalty. If it succeeds, the &quot;victim&quot; gains the ability to use that nightmare for the rest of the scene.The victim can only use the normal effect, and must pay either a willpower point or 2 supernatural fuel points to use the nightmare. Beyond their store of these resources, there is no limit to how often they can use it. The manifestation of the nightmare remain the same as the original beast's, but the beast has no control over how the victim uses their new power, and cannot remove it prematurely.<br /> This nightmare cannot be used on another beast<br /> <br /> <b>High Satiety</b>- The victim uses the nightmare as if at high satiety (this effect remains even if the beast drops in satiety before the nightmare runs out)<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure</b>- The victim can spend double (i.e. two willpower or 4 supernatural fuel points) to use the nightmare's satiety expenditure effect.<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success</b>- The beast is immune to the victim's nightmare, and can make a contested resolve+supernatural resistance to preemptively remove the power if they wish.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12109,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","user":"Urbenmyth","date":". 03-30-2017, 11:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T20:45:47-07:00","id":1071014,"title":"","content":"No comment on the mechanics right now, but I think the ideas behind both of those nightmares are AWESOME!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T05:39:59-07:00","id":1074603,"title":"","content":"Is there a nightmare for stealing social and mental traits from a person, like Merits, skills, successes and Maybe even dots?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T10:37:35-07:00","id":1076577,"title":"","content":"This Will Never Work (Common)<br /> Fear: Nothing you ever do will ever work out for the best.<br /> Roll: Manipulation +Satiety versus Resolve + Tolerance<br /> Action: Target subtracts the higher of either his opponent's Resolve, or his own, to any Contested Rolls. Add 1 to this penalty for Social Rolls.<br /> High Satiety: The target is convinced not only of his personal failures, but in the failure of his connections and institutions. The target cannot use Social Merits that originated from his own efforts; only Social Merits representing help from outside his personal control, such as inherited Resources, a tutor-Mentor paid for by parents and colleagues, or an Artifact temporarily given him by a PC, can aid him. True Friend is explicitly excluded from Socail Merits temporarily blocked out, but the target is at a -2 to contact such persons or ask for help, fearing their 'stench of failure' will spread to them.<br /> SatExpend: The target cannot gain exceptional successes to any action whose primary benefactor is himself. Any aid he might lend to another character is reduced by 1 die (2 die if the person he is attempting to aid is, themselves, undergoing a Nightmare).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I used to know things. Forbidden things.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","name":"Brasstreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar306_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T18:35:49-07:00","id":1076742,"title":"","content":"Because I've been reading princess, and I like the contrast<br /> <br /> <b>There Is No Hope (Dethroned Kinship)</b><br /> <i>Even the incarnations of the light cannot stay the course in this world. Even angels and superheroes fall. What hope do you have? Give up while you still can. Everyone else has, even the Light itself.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Action</b>- Satiety+Manipulation vs Resolve + Supernatural Tolerance<br /> <b>Normal Effect</b>- the victim finds it hard to care. Who cares if you succeed or fail? When spending willpower, the victim only gains half the benefit (that is, a +2 bonus usually)<br /> <b>High Satiety</b>- Sleep becomes fitful, virtues shallow- even vice loses any allure in this world. The victim cannot regain willpower while under the effect of this nightmare<br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure</b>- Do you see how futile it all is, now? The victim is overwhelmed with the horror of the world. They may curl up and weep, collapse into hysterics or just stand staring into space. During this period, they don't respond to any stimuli except that which is directly harmful to them or their motivation, and even that requires either a resolve+composure roll or the spending of a willpower point. While it's beyond mechanics, after this power has worn off being exposed to cosmic despair may have a variety of lingering effects.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success</b>- The victim loses a point of willpower<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>There Is Still Hope</b> <b>(Radiant Princess Kinship)</b><br /> <i>Why haven't you changed the world? I know- it's too hard, you're too small, they're too powerful. But here she is, a shining hero, fighting the good fight and destroying evil. Maybe the world isn't doomed. Maybe evil hasn't won. Maybe it really is that you're just too </i><i>weak</i><i> to step in.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Action</b>- Satiety+Composure vs Resolve + Supernatural Tolerance<br /> <b>Normal Effect</b>- &quot;You have killed 2.338 people&quot; The victim finds justifying their actions harder and harder; the consequences of everything they do spring vividly to mind. The victim cannot regain willpower from their vice(s) while under this power's effect (for mask/dirge, legend/life, blood/bone etc the nightmare may have varying effects- determine based on whether the character sees one, both or neither as their &quot;vice&quot;)<br /> <b>High Satiety</b>- the guilt at the victim's indulgence and apathy is overwhelming in the face of ultimate compassion. When they indulge their vice, they lose a point of willpower instead of gaining it.<br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure</b>- Perhaps there is one last chance to be redeemed, to be approved in her blazing eyes. The beast chooses a cause- anything from &quot;gay rights&quot; to &quot;tidy this room&quot;. It must be something the victim is at least nominally in favour of- if not, the satiety is wasted. The victim goes to extreme lengths to promote this cause. They will stop short at anything that would cause a breaking point or serious harm to themselves, but will otherwise focus on this until the nightmare wears off. Social rolls that fit in with this new dedication start with two less doors.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success</b>- the victim also suffers -1 to breaking point rolls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12109,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","user":"Urbenmyth","date":". 04-11-2017, 10:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T18:53:32-07:00","id":1076745,"title":"","content":"Love the Terry Pratchett reference","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T19:24:46-07:00","id":1076751,"title":"","content":"Turns out I got the quote <i>wrong</i> but hey, the wonders of editing!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T16:27:10-07:00","id":1077325,"title":"","content":"You've Changed (Common)<br /> Fear: People used to like you more in the past/You've lost your edge/You Used To Be Cool<br /> Roll: Intelligence + Satiety vs Compusure + Tolerance<br /> Action: The target feels like those he loves are just going through the motions. Take the Depressed condition for a scene, and reduce the number of Doors needed to convince him of the merits of a 'cool' action by 1.<br /> High Satiety: Increase the duration to a full week.<br /> SatExpend: Make that the Leveraged condition, as the target sees the judging eyes of those he loves as coming from disdain or anger rather than the apathy and progress of time.<br /> Exceptional: The number of Doors is reduced by 2 for the scene. High Satiety still only provides 1 Door for the week.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I used to know things. Forbidden things.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","name":"Brasstreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar306_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T17:46:50-07:00","id":1086900,"title":"","content":"<b>You Can't Trust Your Senses </b>[Common]<br /> <br /> <i>So much of our worldview is shaped by what we can perceive. The slightest disturbance can set us on edge and make us doubt our sanity. How can we function if there is no way to tell the real from the illusory?</i><br /> <br /> <b>Dicepool</b>: Manipulation + Satiety vs Composure + Supernatural Tolerance<br /> <br /> <b>Normal Satiety:</b> The Beast mimics the Hallucination Numen (see Beast: The Primordial, page 194). The illusion lasts for a number of turns equal to Lair.<br /> <br /> <b>High Satiety:</b> The Beast may create a complex illusion that affects all senses, and obeys a number of simple commands equal to Lair. Examples of acceptable commands include &quot;scream when you see that person&quot;, &quot;hide this object&quot; and &quot;leave a trail of blood leading in that direction&quot;. The illusion now lasts for the scene, but cannot affect material reality. The Beast may affect multiple people with these complex illusions, but each one after the first imposes a cumulative -1 penalty.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure: </b>The illusion becomes extremely convincing and striking. The player may spend multiple points of Satiety on this effect. For every point of Satiety spent, the Beast may reflexively cause the victim to fail a single Perception roll. If the Satiety is High, the player may specify which command(s) of the illusion will cause the automatic failure of the Perception roll.<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> The victim gains the Delusional Condition, which makes them believe the illusion was completely real. Alternatively, it makes them believe nothing they perceive can be taken at face value.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T20:48:54-07:00","id":1086985,"title":"","content":"<b>Walking on Eggshells:</b> (mechanics unplanned)<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Don't touch that, you'll break it.&quot;</i> or maybe &quot;<i>You're on thin ice.&quot; </i>Whatever quote you wish to use, the point is the same; this nightmare instills the paranoid sensation that something in the environment is more fragile than it appears; shattering when exposed to pressure from the careless individual. Collectors swear by this Nightmare, claiming that it has been a useful tool in keeping greedy hands off their priceless treasures!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T00:14:28-07:00","id":1087034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=1086900#post1086900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>You Can't Trust Your Senses </b>[Common]<br /> <br /> <i>So much of our worldview is shaped by what we can perceive. The slightest disturbance can set us on edge and make us doubt our sanity. How can we function if there is no way to tell the real from the illusory?</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. Seeing as I'm watching the Framework eps of Agents of SHIELD, this was an interesting writeup for me to see. Nice work on the mechanics, man. So far, I don't see anything out of place with them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T07:17:01-07:00","id":1087662,"title":"","content":"Some slasher nightmares! Because why not.<br /> <br /> <b>The Stories Are Real (Avenger/Legend kinship)</b><br /> <br /> <i>It was never meant to be real. It was just old wives tales and children's stories. But now it's here, just like the story said. Now it's real. How many other terrible things you think are just stories are real, too? </i><br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool</b>: Presence + Satiety vs Resolve + Supernatural Resistance<br /> <br /> <b>Normal Effect</b>: The boundaries between reality, fiction, dreams and fears start to break down for the victim. The victim suffers a -2 penalty to all intelligence skill rolls, as things they learnt, things they heard on the grapevine and outright fiction all spring to mind. In addition, if the victim has Eidetic Memory, they lose its benefits for the duration of the effect.<br /> <br /> <b>High Satiety Effect</b>: The victims grip on reality slips even further, as memories and dreams start to blur together. The victim loses a door in social manoeuvring- even the most empty threats, absurd promises or blatant lies start to seem downright plausible in their dreamlike state.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure</b>- Slipping into legends and myths, they fall to the most obvious one. The victim sees the images of the beast's legend everywhere- a Makara Siren makes the victim hear the seuctive music from every lake and river, the Anakim Troll makes them see looming figures under every bridge. The precise effects of this are not mechanical- how the victim responds is up to them, but is likely to be profound. After the effect ends, the victim only remembers a terrifying dream.<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success</b>- The penalty is -3<br /> <br /> <b>You Can't Talk Your Way Out Of This (Brute/Mask kinship)</b><br /> <br /> <i>You think you're powerful? Charming, wealthy, connected? But here, your words fall on deaf ears. Here, your money is just paper and scrap metal. Here, your laws have no power. You can't run, can't fight. Do you still think you're powerful?</i><br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool</b>: Presence + Satiety vs Composure + Supernatural Resistance<br /> <br /> <b>Normal Effect</b>: In the face of silent brutality, the so-called &quot;power&quot; of society seems useless. The victim must roll resolve+composure to use social merits that rely on connections or social standing (E.g. Status, Resources, Allies, Contacts). Social merits that rely on inherent nature (e.g.Pusher, Striking Looks, Closed Book) can be used normally.<br /> <br /> <b>High Satiety Effect</b>: The petty to-and-fros of humanity mean nothing before brute force. The victim cannot use soft leverage for the duration of the nightmare- they must either use brutality or rely on luck.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure</b>- Words words words. They will do nothing. The victim can no longer speak or write, and even hand gestures beyond flailing become impossible. Mechanics wise, they suffer from a Mask's &quot;No Mind But For Murder&quot; frailty for the remainder of the scene.<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success</b>: Even inherent social merits need the roll- what use is beauty or calmness against an axe to the face?<br /> <br /> <b>It Could Be Anyone (Charmer/Psycho kinship)</b><br /> <br /> <i>The kindly old man running the store. The pretty lady at the bar. The charming new face in town. That couple, that kid. Your best friend. How many of them are hiding knifes behind their smiles...and how can you ever know?</i><br /> <br /> <b>Dice Poll</b>: Manipulation + Satiety vs Resolve + Supernatural Resistance<br /> <br /> <b>Normal Effect</b>- Anyone could be a monster- why focus on the Beast? The Beast blurs into the crowd- if there are at least a dozen people around, all attempts by the victim to notice, recognise or remember the beast's appearance suffer a -2 penalty.<br /> <br /> <b>High Satiety Effect</b>- The people who help you, who control you, who hold your life in their hand- can you trust them? The Beast appears to the victim as a person of authority- maybe they seem to be a learned professor, a agent of the law or a medical professional. This gives them a +2 bonus to any checks that perception could help, and also makes them hard to remember- the victim just remembers &quot;a cop&quot; or &quot;a doctor&quot; with no other details.<br /> (note, this can have penalties too- if the victim is a gangster, say, appearing as a &quot;police officer&quot; may well backfire)<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure</b>- No-one is safe. No-one. The Beast appears as someone the victim knows. If they are aware of a specific person, they can choose to appear as them. If not, they can guess a type of person- &quot;your best friend&quot;, &quot;your boss&quot;, &quot;your child&quot;- although if no-one fits that category the satiety is wasted.<br /> <br /> Under this power, the beast's appears as the person to all senses automatically copies mannerisms. They do not need to act &quot;in character&quot; to preserve the effect, although if they act wildly different the victim may get an intelligence check (and likely a breaking point) to figure out the truth<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success</b>- the beast is very vague. Even if the victim notices them, they are unable to give any further details.<br /> <br /> <b>You Could Have Stopped This (Freak/Mutant kinship)</b><br /> <br /> <i>It didn't have to be this way. If you'd shown an ounce of kindness or acceptance. If you'd treated them like a human being, just once. But you didn't. You shunned the freak and cast them into the dark. You created a monster. And now it's here for you.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Dice Poll</b>- Wits + Satiety vs Resolve + Supernatural Resistance<br /> <br /> <b>Normal Effect</b>- after all you've done, you at least owe it the truth. The victim cannot lie to the beast, nor can they resort to clever wordplay or half-truths. At best, they can refuse to answer a question or make genuine mistakes<br /> <br /> <b>High Satiety Effect</b>- You have already hurt it enough. The victim suffers a -2 penalty to any attempts to attack or directly hurt the beast.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure</b>- Atone for your crime, one way or another. The beast can make a single request of the victim- this request can be anything possible to do. Upon doing this, the victim has two choices. They can grant the request. If they refuse (or agree with no intention of actually going through with it, or otherwise try and get around it), they immediately suffer a number of points of lethal damage equal to the Beasts Satiety, as their flesh is ripped apart by invisible claws. Either way, they are now free from the effects of the nightmare.<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success</b>- the victim must make a resolve+composure roll to avoid answering a direct question from the beast.<br /> <br /> <b>Nothing Is Safe (Genius/Maniac kinship)</b><br /> <br /> <i>That food could be poisoned. That door sabotaged. That friend compromised, that machine hacked, that house rigged to blow. Anything. It's so much smarter then you, after all. How could you ever see its traps coming?</i><br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool</b>- Manipulation + Satiety vs Composure + Supernatural Resistance.<br /> <br /> <b>Normal Effect</b>- It's all trapped, all wired. The victim must make a resolve+Composure roll to go to any place they haven't been before for the duration of the nightmare<br /> <br /> <b>High Satiety Effect</b>- Bribery. Blackmail. Intimidation. There's so many ways it can turn your friends against you. The victim suffers the Paranoia condition for the rest of the scene (the sign should be something related to the slasher the kinship was gained from)<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure</b>- you think you've cracked the code. You think you know how to be safe. Choose an activity- for the remainder of the scene, the victim will refuse to do that thing under any circumstances. This choice can't be deadly (&quot;breathing&quot;) or totally debilitating (&quot;moving&quot;) but otherwise anything will work. If the victim is forced to perform that activity, they immediately suffer a breaking point and will take any efforts necessary to stop until they do or the power wears off.<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success</b>- the victim must make the roll to leave their current area at all- who knows what might have happened while they weren't looking?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12109,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","user":"Urbenmyth","date":". 05-04-2017, 11:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T23:26:51-07:00","id":1088124,"title":"","content":"I don't know how well this would actually work, or if it fits thematically. But it could be kinda cool to have a sort of nightmare that forces a &quot;mental duel&quot; with another, to get to invoke a &quot;bossfight&quot; even if you can't do all your lair opening tricks. &quot;battle in the center of the mind&quot; style. I don't have good mechanical idea how to do it, outside of literally making it into a duel of some kind (with maybe high satiety beast being able to project his beasts dream form instead of himself to another because he can visualise it easier with clear head.). <br /> <br /> <b>This is between you and me</b><br /> <i>You thought you could muster your strength, prepare, gather up your allies. You had assets, backup plans, friends. Those cannot help you now, you are on your own. Stand with your own two feet, or perish like all those before you.</i><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12705-xararion","name":"Xararion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T10:35:16-07:00","id":1090353,"title":"","content":"<b>You've Already Lost (Princess Kinship)</b><br /> You can fight and fight and fight to change things, but the world won't bend for one person, and the war was won long ago by the other side. To persist is pointless.<br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Presence + Satiety vs. Resolve + Supernatural Resistance; Nobles can substitute Belief for Inner Light<br /> <br /> <b>Normal Effect:</b> The war is lost and fighting is pointless. Your victim cannot spend Willpower for the rest of the scene.<br /> <br /> <b>High Satiety:</b> The weight of inevitable failure crushes the life out of your victim, inflicting the Beaten Down tilt.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> Your victim has been so thoroughly crushed, they suffer the Insensate tilt.<br /> <br /> <b>Hell is Other People (Paragon Genius Kinship)</b><br /> People are chained by the eyes of others, the morality placed upon them by their society, and the taboo of society. Even if you're alone, you feel the eyes of others judging you.<br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Manipulation + Satiety vs. Resolve + Supernatural Resistance<br /> <br /> <b>Normal Effect:</b> The victim feels the eyes of society on them. They must spend a point of Willpower the first time they take an action that breaks taboo or social custom, even if it would normally be morally justifiable.<br /> <br /> <b>High Satiety:</b> The victim is found wanting by even themselves. In addition to spending Willpower, the victim suffers the Guilty tilt after breaking taboo.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> For the rest of the scene, the victim has &quot;Breaking social custom&quot; as a Breaking Point.<br /> <br /> <b>My Beloved (Leviathan's Beloved Kinship)</b><br /> She didn't understand why she felt that way, but she needed the creature. She needed to <i>belong</i> to it, and knew it would need her in return.<br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Presence + Satiety vs. Composure + Supernatural Resistance<br /> <br /> <b>Normal Effect:</b> You become an island of solace for your victim. Your victim receives one extra DOT of Willpower while in your presence. they must spend a point of Willpower to leave.<br /> <br /> <b>High Satiety:</b> Your victim needs you and only you. They acquire the Addicted condition to your presence.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> Your victim has been given a permanent place in your soul, literally. For the rest of the story, the victim is immune to the hazards of your Lair, and must return to your Lair once per chapter or suffer a Breaking Point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T13:28:47-07:00","id":1090458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=1090353#post1090353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>My Beloved (Leviathan's Beloved Kinship)</b><br /> She didn't understand why she felt that way, but she needed the creature. She needed to <i>belong</i> to it, and knew it would need her in return.<br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Presence + Satiety vs. Composure + Supernatural Resistance<br /> <br /> <b>Normal Effect:</b> You become an island of solace for your victim. Your victim receives one extra DOT of Willpower while in your presence. they must spend a point of Willpower to leave.<br /> <br /> <b>High Satiety:</b> Your victim needs you and only you. They acquire the Addicted condition to your presence.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> Your victim has been given a permanent place in your soul, literally. For the rest of the story, the victim is immune to the hazards of your Lair, and must return to your Lair once per chapter or suffer a Breaking Point.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this one. Both for the creepiness and for the way that it actually plays into the Heroes' narrative: the Beast actually<i> did</i> lay an enchantment on the 'fair maiden'.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T05:28:08-07:00","id":1093626,"title":"","content":"In a Striking Coincidence I made a Duchagne Kinship Nightmare which is similar in concept to You Can't Trust Your Senses but it worked differently:<br /> <br /> <b>Your Senses Cannot be Trusted</b><br /> <i>What was that? Did that really just happen or is it inside the confines of your own mind. Your friends didn\u2019t flinch but you know you felt the brush of fire across your cheek. The smell of ashes, the taste of your own blood.</i><br /> <b>Dice Pool: </b>Satiety + Intelligence vs Resolve + Supernatural Tolerance<br /> <b>Normal: </b>The Beast nominates one of the victim\u2019s senses when invoking the Nightmare. The victim is plagued by persistent false inputs that conform to the Beast\u2019s nature. All of a victims food might taste like it is slightly spoiled or they may hear ringing sounds after loud noises. They begin to lose trust in the particular sense affected, second guessing whether or not what they have experienced is real. The Victim takes a -2 penalty to any roll that relies on the affected sense.<br /> <b>High Satiety: </b>A content Beast can linger upon the suffering of the victim, directing the hallucinations to influence the characters behaviour. The Beast can choose to associate the unpleasant hallucinations with certain people, places or behaviours or to exempt a specific stimulus from them. Over time this leads the victim to develop a Condition pertaining to the stimulus. The character either gains the Spooked Condition toward the source of the hallucinations or the Swooned Condition in regards to the one thing that is exempt from them.<br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure: </b>There are few fears as deeply engrained or as often forgotten as losing one\u2019s senses. It\u2019s almost a joke to parents to say; \u201cdon\u2019t touch yourself or you will go blind.\u201d But losing your sight is terrifying to those who have gone through it and is often the beginning of a life of being ignored by the world at large. Instead of suffering from confused input the Victim of the nightmare loses the chosen sense entirely.<br /> <br /> Blindness, Deafness \u2013 The character takes a -5 Penalty to all actions that rely upon the missing sense. If another sense can be reasonably used instead, such as a blind person navigating by sound or a deaf person reading lips, this is reduced to a -3 instead.<br /> <br /> Analgesia \u2013 The character cannot feel their skin or extremities. They have no tactile sensation and if cut or burned they do not realise so until they see the wound. They do not suffer wound penalties but also take a -3 penalty to any actions that would be impeded by this drawback \u2013 such as touch typing or chopping vegetables.<br /> <br /> Insensate \u2013 The character cannot smell or taste anything at all; rendering the act of eating a joyless thing. They take no penalties from environmental effects that rely on smell, such as a noxious odour, but at the cost of general unhappiness. In a scene where the character has eaten or drunk in company with others they take a -3 penalty to all Social dice rolls.<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success: </b>When invoking the Nightmare the Beast can choose to affect two senses instead of one. For the purpose of the High Satiety affect the two senses are still treated as linked to the same stimulus.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The ego is not king of its own castle.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13329-strictura","name":"Strictura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13329_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T07:46:36-07:00","id":1093655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strictura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=1093626#post1093626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Snip.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very nice, especially for a newcomer to the forums. I liked your merit as well. It's good to see someone new.<br /> <br /> P.S. I love your signature. Very insightful. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T22:52:31-07:00","id":1094002,"title":"","content":"Hey guys,<br /> <br /> New to the forum and Beast. This is my first attempt at a homebrew nightmare. I workshopped it with Strictura XD. This is a kinship nightmare based on a demon in my chronicle that I am running.<br /> <br /> I See You [Analyst, Demon Kinship]<br /> <br /> Dice Pool: None, see below.<br /> Action: Reflexive<br /> <br /> Normal: The Beast takes a -2 penalty on her roll to invoke another Nightmare. He does not need to lock eyes or touch the target as long as her intended victim can be remotely viewed using a camera or similar device. All that is needed to invoke the nightmare is that the victim look into the lens (or similar apparatus) while the Beast can see them.<br /> <br /> High Satiety: As Normal, but the victim does not need to look into the camera and does not even have to consciously know they are being observed.<br /> <br /> Satiety Expenditure: Once the Nightmare is successfully invoked the Beast may choose to spend a point of Satiety to make a recording of the victim as they suffer its effects. This can be visual, audio or a combination of the two. If the victim sees or hears the recording they must make a Resolve + Composure roll or fall victim to the same nightmare again. Furthermore, if someone other than the original victim experiences the recording in the Beasts presence the Beast may spend Satiety again to force them to make the same roll and suffer the Nightmare.<br /> <br /> If any victim scores an Exceptional Success on this resistance roll the Nightmare is rendered inert and can no longer be used to affect further targets.<br /> <br /> Exceptional Success: Anyone experiencing the recording is subject to the Exceptional Success result of the original nightmare.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot;To succeed, planning alone is insufficient. One must improvise as well.&quot; - Salvor Hardin, Foundation</span></span></span></div>","edited":{"userid":13444,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13444-zannmato","user":"zannmato","date":". 05-18-2017, 05:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13444-zannmato","name":"zannmato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-20T02:55:36-07:00","id":1094821,"title":"","content":"The idea itself is neat, but I believe demons are specifically listed as &quot;not of the blood&quot; and cannot be made kinships with due to the inherent animosity demons and beasts feel towards each other. I actually like the expenditure version of making a &quot;haunted dvd&quot; more than I do the actual &quot;I can aim my nightmare from anywhere&quot;, since the -2 seems kinda low penalty when high satiety version would let you essentially strike nightmares across any distance from simple webcam or conference call that's live.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12705-xararion","name":"Xararion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T15:00:09-07:00","id":1095253,"title":"","content":"Thanks man. Yes you are absolutley right. my justification for having this kind of nightnare in my story is that, despite being unable to establish family ties with demons, I still feel that beasts can see the fear that demons create in humans and use it, plus I love demon XD. I agree that I should change the high satiety effect, I'll repost once I've changed it, maybe I can limit the normal effect aswell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot;To succeed, planning alone is insufficient. One must improvise as well.&quot; - Salvor Hardin, Foundation</span></span></span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13444-zannmato","name":"zannmato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T17:13:23-07:00","id":1095296,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13444-zannmato\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar13444_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13444\" data-vbnamecard=\"13444\">zannmato</a> Your &quot;I See You&quot; Nightmare could come from Kinship with Mastigos Mages. I can also see it as a Common Nightmare, since the feeling of being watched by someone or something that wants to harm you is scary in an archetypal way. You could also check out the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=833241#post833241\"><b>In My Image</b></a> Atavism for inspiration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T23:31:07-07:00","id":1095385,"title":"","content":"Irraka werewolves, Darkling changelings, and Mekhet and Nosferatu could also qualify for the Nightmare in terms of Kinship.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-24T22:49:01-07:00","id":1096618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=1095385#post1095385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Irraka werewolves, Darkling changelings, and Mekhet and Nosferatu could also qualify for the Nightmare in terms of Kinship.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd completely forgotten about Iron Masters in werewolf. Irraka is such a great idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot;To succeed, planning alone is insufficient. One must improvise as well.&quot; - Salvor Hardin, Foundation</span></span></span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13444-zannmato","name":"zannmato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-24T23:02:44-07:00","id":1096623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zannmato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=1096618#post1096618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd completely forgotten about Iron Masters in werewolf. Irraka is such a great idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah. Iron Masters also make sense, and I'd also throw in Bone Shadows and Hunters in Darkness as other possible sources. Maybe even Fire-Touched, too?<br /> <br /> In terms of other splats, Jackal-Headed mummies and Geists/Sin-Eaters may also qualify as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T07:11:43-07:00","id":1118527,"title":"","content":"This needs balancing, any ideas?<br /> <br /> <u><b>This isn't real!</b></u>Changeling/Mastigos Kinship)<br /> <i>Are you sure this world is real? </i><br /> <b>Roll</b>: Intelligence + Satiety vs. Composure + Supernatural Tolerance<br /> <b>Effect</b>: The Victim suffers the Delusion condition, becoming convinced that the world he inhabits is just a simulation/illusion/dream etc., and a nagging feeling that he needs to get out. ST decides what method the Victim feels is the way to freedom from the following list (advance as needed):<br /> Escape the area, jump from a high building, harm yourself (Either 1B or 1L), experience an intense sensation for a strong enough 'kick' (e.g.falling, pain, or water), destroy a certain object, convince someone else of the 'Truth', make someone go to a place, perform a certain action at a certain place (e.g. open and close every drawer twice) etc.<br /> The Victim can resist obviously dangerous activities like 'jump from a high building' with an uncontested Resolve+Composure roll + Bonus depending on the threat level (kill yourself would yield +5, harm yourself +1). If they fail, they will take actions into the necessary direction. If they don't fail, they will search for a way to do this safely, e.g. get a parachute, have a friend close-by to resuscitate them etc.<br /> After having performed the action, the Nightmare ends.<br /> <b>High Satiety effect</b>: The Beast chooses what the Victim believes in, and how they believe to be able to escape. In addition, the victim's social rolls are penalized by -3, because to their mind, they do not deal with real people, and treat them accordingly. Futhermore, having performed the action does not end the Nightmare, and the Victim becomes convinced they did something wrong and try again. This could mean escape a larger Area (Building-&gt; Block-&gt; City), experience a stronger sensation (higher, faster), harming themselves again etc.<br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure</b>: Dreams have Projections, The Matrix has Agents. Whatever the means, the Victim is convinced that people trying to stop them from leaving are not real, and thus has no qualms in resorting to disproportionate violence. Upon the end of the Nightmare, Breaking Points are rolled as normal. Furthermore, the Victim feels that time is running out: the closer they get to the Nightmare ending, the more desperate and frantic they get to achieve their goal.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success</b>: Doing anything that does not advance the goal suffers a -2 Penalty.<br /> <br /> <br /> Need some help with the next one, too<br /> <u><b>This is what you really are</b></u> (Common)<br /> <i>Sometimes, the scariest things are not something in the corner of your eye, or what can be done to you by others. Sometimes, acknowledging yourself, realizing your weaknesses and being unable to deny your flaws is what breaks people. Let's lend them a helping hand, shall we?</i><br /> <b>Roll</b>: Intelligence+ Satiety vs. Resolve + Supernatural Tolerance<br /> <b>Effect</b>: The Victim is drawn towards his flaws and feels drained acting against them. Acting according to their Vice yields double the reward, whereas acting according to their Virtue costs one Willpower.<br /> <b>High Satiety effect</b>: The Victim acts compulsively whenever faced with a situation where they could sate their Vice. Roll Resolve+Composure-Beast's Lair to determine whether they manage to not give in. This stacks with the Normal Effect. <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure</b>: Anyone an idea for this?<br /> <b>Exceptional Success</b>: Same here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T19:07:12-07:00","id":1121665,"title":"","content":"In a game I'm helping run (discord-type 'chat' game), the local Begotten in the city have been 'welcomed' into the Vampiric Court, and as a special little bonus, if they get Covenant status, instead of getting vampiric powers, they count as automatically having Family Ties to Vampires of that Covenant. So, I made one for each of the primary Covenants so there's something for players to start with:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <b>Your boss brings me my lunch (Invictus Vampire)</b><br /> <br /> <i>Don't you know him? He's the one that's always in -those- meetings, isn't he? What does he want with you? What could he possibly need? And what's going to happen to you if you refuse him?</i><br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Manipulation + Satiety vs Resolve + Supernatural Tolerance<br /> <b>Normal:</b> The victim becomes convinced that the Beast is his superior, either in a named group or organization the Beast knows they have status in, or just in a general uneasy feeling that the Beast has some sway over him. Mechanically, the Beast is treated as having 1 more dot in (mundane) status than the victim in the applicable group for the sake of social benefits and perceived authority, or else the victim simply takes the Leveraged condition applying to the Beast, resolving it normally.<br /> <b>High Satiety:</b> The effect of the Beast's apparent authority becomes more direct. In addition to the above, the victim has one fewer door in social maneuvering attempts from the Beast, and will never drop below an Average impression.<br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> By spending Satiety, the Beast may duplicate Supernatural status (and equivalents, like Mantle and Renown), even if the victim knows full well the Beast couldn't have it. For instance, when dealing with a Changeling in the Ash Court, he gains the social benefit of having a dot more of Mantle than the victim (but no other bonus from it).<br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> The Beast is treated as having <i>2</i> more dots than the victim, or else also applies the Guilty condition (as the victim gains the nagging feeling that they've <i>already</i> earned the Beast's ire).<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Don't abuse your power (Carthian Vampire)</b><br /> <br /> <i>They're at the door. They know who you are, and they don't care. They're going to get in, they're going to find you, and they're going to stop you from abusing your power any longer. The only way to stop it is to give it up altogether.</i><br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Wits + Satiety vs Composure + Supernatural Tolerance<br /> <b>Normal:</b> The victim becomes convinced that he's stood on his title or position for too long, and it's going to bite him in the ass. Any social rolls he makes, whether his own or resisting another's actions, take a -2 penalty if he has higher Status than the other character in the same organization (lacking status altogether doesn't count), and he loses the normal dice bonus from the status as well. This lasts for a full 24 hours.<br /> <b>High Satiety:</b> The victim actually effectively loses his status in a specified group for the duration, as he becomes unwilling to pull any strings, go to any meetings, or otherwise make his presence known among the organization.<br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> The victim will levy a favor or other use of his Status for the Beast, becoming convinced that doing so will keep others off his back. This must be something typically possible for his status level, not something that would risk the status long term.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> The effect lasts for a week.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>What's with this place? (Ordo Dracul Vampire)</b><br /> <br /> <i>There's something about this place. What, what was that? It doesn't feel right. It's almost like there's something here. Something wrong. Something\u2026 unnatural.</i><br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Intelligence + Satiety vs Composure + Supernatural Tolerance<br /> <b>Normal:</b> The victim becomes extra-sensitive to the resonance of supernatural locations. Whenever present within a Haunted locale, spiritual nexus, or other \u201cWyrm's Nest\u201d (as the Ordo Vampires call it), the victim takes the Spooked condition, immediately becoming aware that something's <i>wrong</i> with the place. If present at the time, the Beast becomes inherently aware that the victim has sensed something.<br /> <b>High Satiety:</b> The victim takes on the Obsessed condition relating to the location for the duration, gaining the usual benefits for looking into or studying it. It cannot be resolved until after the Nightmare's duration ends.<br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> When sensing the victim's Spooked condition, the Beast may spend a Satiety to gain a flash of empathic intuition regarding the nature of the fear; this effectively provides insight into the nature of the Nest. A Haunt might reveal a flash of the ghost out of the corner of the victim's eye, or the feeling of the chill of the grave, whereas a Mage's Hallow might cause a sensation of inferiority and wrongness about themselves.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> The power lasts for a full 24 hours.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>You are Unworthy (Lancea et Sanctum Vampire)</b><br /> <br /> <i>He's watching you. He knows you're unworthy. You need to prove yourself. You have to show Him that you can reflect His glory.</i><br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Manipulation + Satiety vs Resolve + Supernatural Tolerance<br /> <b>Normal:</b> The victim becomes filled with a feeling of inadequacy, and they feel as if the Beast is the only one who can help redeem them. For the duration, they suffer a -2 penalty to all actions, UNLESS they're either assisting the Beast in some way, or doing something they know the Beast wants, in which case the penalty instead becomes a +2 bonus.<br /> <b>High Satiety:</b> In teamwork actions with the Beast as the leader, the victim's efforts grant the Beast the 8-again quality on their own roll, so long as they've rolled at least a single success.<br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> By spending a Satiety, the victim gains the 8-again benefit on any rolls meant to protect the Beast from some form of harm or hostility, lest their one potential method of redemption be lost.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> The penalty/bonus becomes 3 dice.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>You're a Monster Too (Circle of the Crone Vampire)</b><br /> <br /> <i>What's that working through your blood? It feels primal. Powerful. Monstrous. But\u2026 good. Why does it feel so good? What can you possibly do but unleash it?</i><br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> None, see below<br /> <b>Action:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Normal:</b> The Beast takes a -2 penalty to invoke another Nightmare on the target (who can choose not to resist), but instead of it taking effect, the victim becomes capable of unleashing the Nightmare for the Beast, on a target of their own choosing. Doing so requires them to suffer 1L damage, which manifests as a deep laceration on their body as the 'magic' escapes them. The effect works the same as if the Beast themself had utilized it with the same number of successes originally rolled.<br /> <b>High Satiety:</b> The victim unleashes the Nightmare's High Satiety effect.<br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> The victim unleashes the Nightmare's Satiety Expenditure effect, and suffers no damage to do so.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> As per the invoked Nightmare.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> Tried to expand things a little to let some act as 'buffs' of sorts as the book hinted is possible (but didn't provide any examples of, if I recall).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> On another note, I've been pondering a Changeling Kinship Nightmare that at Normal Satiety gives you glimpses of their dreams as they see images of you in their sleep (which grants some minor bonuses), at High Satiety gives you direct ingress, and with Satiety Expenditure counts their dreams as part of your Lair for that night, for all intents and purposes. Something I may toy with.<br /> Also opens the possibility of then permanently creating a Chamber out of a Dream, though that might be arguably impossible since dreams fade away each morning and all, and might not be in the same place metaphysically speaking otherwise. Still, it could make for an interesting merit or just special system. I suppose I'm still hoping that the player's guide will cover more ways to directly interact with dreams.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T11:15:06-07:00","id":1123086,"title":"","content":"Did any Nightmare here pull the target's Dream Form into the Beast's Lair, for any of it's effects? Or is that an open niche? (Probably best used for triggering &quot;When the Target next goes to sleep&quot;)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-25T11:20:16-07:00","id":1143849,"title":"","content":"Not that I know of. Anyway, someone joked around about a &quot;You Can't Kill It&quot; Nightmare on another thread and it made me think about making one. My thought is it inflicts the Beaten Down tilt, even on supernatural opponents it doesn't apply to. Opposed by Supernatural Resistance of course. I'm not sure how to flesh it out though. Any ideas?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-25T11:50:30-07:00","id":1143852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=1143849#post1143849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not that I know of. Anyway, someone joked around about a &quot;You Can't Kill It&quot; Nightmare on another thread</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2026That's not a joke. You Cannot Kill It is one of the sample Kinship Nightmares. It makes the target only able to do bashing damage to you without Anathema, gives a negative modifier to their weapon damage with High Satiety, and costs them a point of Willpower every time they fail an attack roll against you on an Exceptional Success.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-25T13:05:23-07:00","id":1143876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=1143852#post1143852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026That's not a joke. You Cannot Kill It is one of the sample Kinship Nightmares. It makes the target only able to do bashing damage to you without Anathema, gives a negative modifier to their weapon damage with High Satiety, and costs them a point of Willpower every time they fail an attack roll against you on an Exceptional Success.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh. Still sounds more like an atavism","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-25T13:14:39-07:00","id":1143880,"title":"","content":"What Satchel said. I quoted the core book in the thread in question in response.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i><u><b>You cannot look down</b></u> (Common)</i><br /> Man+Satiety vs. Composure+Supernatural Tolerance<br /> Falling a certain distance kills you, which is why the Body got good at warning you that certain heights are dangerous.<br /> <b>Normal Effect</b>: Everything that is further down than a floor registers as a fall that would result in death to the Body and Triggers the appropriate Response: the victim suffers from the Acrophobic Condition.<br /> <br /> <b>High Satiety</b>: The victim suffers vertigo as even shallow differences in depth grow before their eyes. The normal effect applies even to the height difference in staircase steps. Futhermore, even the most simple falls (e.g. from a chair) deal at least 1 Bashing damage due to the nightmare (in Addition to whatever the fall would have), regardless of mitigating abilities.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure</b>: Your mind makes it real. When confronted with a height difference that causes fear, every Action other than getting away is penalized by -3 as avoiding potential death is at the victim's mind's Forefront. Upgrade any falling damage (including the 1B of this nightmare when applicable) to 1L.<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success</b>: In Addition, the victim suffers from the Sick tilt every time they have to look down at least 1 floor, for 6-Victim's Resolve turns.<br /> <br /> Acrophobic is basically Agoraphobic, replacing wide open spaces and masses of People with heights.<br /> <br /> <i><u><b>You cannot scream</b></u> (Common)</i><br /> Int+Satiety vs. Composure + Supernatural Tolerance<br /> Everyone knows it: the horrible Moment you want to say something, but can't. Losing the ability to talk is a common horror Scenario in dreams for a reason: we are social animals that have a Need to communicate. Losing the main means of doing so is akin to Mutilation, a deep-rooted fear.<br /> <b>Normal</b>: Words won't come out as needed or wanted, getting stuck in the victim's throat or staying at the tip of their tongue. Stuttering becomes commonplace. Actions that require speech are penalized by -2.<br /> <br /> <b>High Satiety</b>: Talking becomes incredibly hard, as the victim needs to fight down the Silence. The victim needs to expend one WP to roll for Actions that require speech (e.g. Persuasion). This is in Addition to the normal effect.<br /> <br /> <b>SatExp: </b>The victim loses the ability to talk or produce Sound of any Kind - they suffer the Mute Condition. Roll Resolve+Composure to determine whether this causes a panic attack.<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional success</b>: Increase the Penalty to -4<br /> <br /> <br /> <u><b><i>You are Soul-Bound! </i></b></u><i>(Dunno, Acanthus Kinship? Mastigos, maybe?)</i><br /> Manipulation+Satiety vs Composure+Supernatural Tolerance<br /> When it gets hurt, you feel the pain.<br /> <b>Normal:</b> Half the Damage dealt to the beast, rounded up is also dealt the Victim of the Nightmare, so long as the Victim can see them.<br /> <br /> <b>High Satiety:</b> The Victim recieves any damage the Beast would normally recieve, and the beast takes only half damage instead..<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> The Beast may Chose to bond someone else to the Victim in their place.<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> for the next [Lair] turns, all damage the Beast (or Placeholder) would recieve is transferred completely to the victim.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":". 09-26-2017, 10:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T13:20:59-07:00","id":1144184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=1143880#post1143880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i><u><b>You cannot scream</b></u> (Common)</i><br /> Int+Satiety vs. Composure + Supernatural Tolerance<br /> Everyone knows it: the horrible Moment you want to say something, but can't. Losing the ability to talk is a common horror Scenario in dreams for a reason: we are social animals that have a Need to communicate. Losing the main means of doing so is akin to Mutilation, a deep-rooted fear.<br /> <b>Normal</b>: Words won't come out as needed or wanted, getting stuck in the victim's throat or staying at the tip of their tongue. Stuttering becomes commonplace. Actions that require speech are penalized by -2.<br /> <br /> <b>High Satiety</b>: Talking becomes incredibly hard, as the victim needs to fight down the Silence. The victim needs to expend one WP to roll for Actions that require speech (e.g. Persuasion). This is in Addition to the normal effect.<br /> <br /> <b>SatExp: </b>The victim loses the ability to talk or produce Sound of any Kind - they suffer the Mute Condition. Roll Resolve+Composure to determine whether this causes a panic attack.<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional success</b>: Increase the Penalty to -4</div> </div> </div> </div>This is my new favorite homebrew nightmare. Kudo <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3648-nepher","name":"Nepher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3648_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T14:21:08-07:00","id":1144195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nepher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=1144184#post1144184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is my new favorite homebrew nightmare. Kudo <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I second that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T14:27:18-07:00","id":1144198,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3648-nepher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3648_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3648\" data-vbnamecard=\"3648\">Nepher</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8180\" data-vbnamecard=\"8180\">Deionscribe</a> Thanks! Glad to hear you like it. Hope it serves your stories well =D","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T13:57:11-07:00","id":1144927,"title":"","content":"Do you think we should ask for this thread to be pinned?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T14:05:40-07:00","id":1144936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=1144927#post1144927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you think we should ask for this thread to be pinned?</div> </div> </div> </div>A homebrew hub, like in the Vampire forum, would be far better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3648-nepher","name":"Nepher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3648_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T15:11:56-07:00","id":1144984,"title":"","content":"Okay, so I need help with two specific nightmare ideas that I want to realize...<br /> <br /> One would be something akin to &quot;You are a beacon&quot;<br /> The fluffy idea is: You are a weirdness Magnet - there is just something about you that draws decidedly unwanted attention.<br /> <br /> <br /> The other idea is &quot;all downhill from here&quot;.<br /> <br /> This is it. This is going to be your <i>greatest </i>achievement. <i>Ever</i>.<br /> However, that also means that the rest of your life is downhill from here. You have peaked, and are doomed to know that <i>nothing will ever fulfill you ever again</i>.<br /> <br /> <br /> And this one needs some help, too:<br /> <br /> <b>You can see dead People! </b>(Ghost, Sin-Eater or Moros Kinship)<br /> Ghosts aren't real. You keep telling that to yourself, because that is the only way to feel comfortable and secure. Not being able to see them helps.<br /> You will never feel save again when you realize they are all around you. Especially not when one of them takes you out for a ride, trying to resolve some business maybe.<br /> Int+Sat vs Res+ST<br /> <br /> <b>Normal</b>: The victim of the nightmare has the Anchor Condition and can now see ghosts within a radius of 10 meters of themselves, and is Aware of their supernatural nature. Ghosts within this perimeter are Aware of this, and the fact that the victim functions like an Anchor.<br /> <br /> <b>High Satiety</b>: In addition, Ghosts can physically interact with the Victim without having to manifest.<br /> <br /> <b>SatExpend</b>: The Victim furthermore gets the Open Condition.<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional success</b>: the Radius increases to 20 Meters.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T21:41:15-07:00","id":1151208,"title":"","content":"Hey ! So I did that. I still have to add the names of contributors, but I think I got all the fully fleshed out Nightmares.<br /> Do you think I should do one with the rule-less ideas ?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/171WcEFKakQxV8ovaPfrDDqQLtQacCfxK-eJdEjpcYpI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/171WcEFKakQxV8ovaPfrDDqQLtQacCfxK-eJdEjpcYpI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/171WcEFKakQxV8ovaPfrDDqQLtQacCfxK-eJdEjpcYpI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/171WcEFKakQxV8ovaPfrDDqQLtQacCfxK-eJdEjpcYpI/edit?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11431-adrasalieth","name":"Adrasalieth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T23:45:00-07:00","id":1151228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Adrasalieth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=1151208#post1151208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey ! So I did that. I still have to add the names of contributors, but I think I got all the fully fleshed out Nightmares.<br /> Do you think I should do one with the rule-less ideas ?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/171WcEFKakQxV8ovaPfrDDqQLtQacCfxK-eJdEjpcYpI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/171WcEFKakQxV8ovaPfrDDqQLtQacCfxK-eJdEjpcYpI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/171WcEFKakQxV8ovaPfrDDqQLtQacCfxK-eJdEjpcYpI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/171WcEFKakQxV8ovaPfrDDqQLtQacCfxK-eJdEjpcYpI/edit?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>That would be good. Perhaps make the document commentable?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-20T07:19:24-07:00","id":1151302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Adrasalieth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=1151208#post1151208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey ! So I did that. I still have to add the names of contributors, but I think I got all the fully fleshed out Nightmares.<br /> Do you think I should do one with the rule-less ideas ?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/171WcEFKakQxV8ovaPfrDDqQLtQacCfxK-eJdEjpcYpI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/171WcEFKakQxV8ovaPfrDDqQLtQacCfxK-eJdEjpcYpI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/171WcEFKakQxV8ovaPfrDDqQLtQacCfxK-eJdEjpcYpI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/171WcEFKakQxV8ovaPfrDDqQLtQacCfxK-eJdEjpcYpI/edit?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>I like this very, very much.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-20T08:30:24-07:00","id":1151333,"title":"","content":"The first document is now open to modifications. Here's the other document, with some Nightmares prompts yet without mechanics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1iJ_UhsBq_pUWtmIprlfPEBLaB_m4YbOgQ6555jQSK0k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1iJ_UhsBq_pUWtmIprlfPEBLaB_m4YbOgQ6555jQSK0k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1iJ_UhsBq_pUWtmIprlfPEBLaB_m4YbOgQ6555jQSK0k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1iJ_UhsBq_pUWtmIprlfPEBLaB_m4YbOgQ6555jQSK0k/edit?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11431-adrasalieth","name":"Adrasalieth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-11T05:00:24-07:00","id":1194211,"title":"","content":"<u><b>You Are Not Beyond Reach (Mage kinship)</b></u><br /> <i>You've boarded yourself in and you've got your gun, but you know </i>it<i> can still get you. It can sink its fingers into you from miles away, and there's nothing you can do to stop it.</i><br /> <b>Normal Effect: </b>To use this Nightmare, the Beast must destroy a sympathetic link to the target - a strand of hair, a drop of blood or some similar link - in a simple rite taking at least a minute - maybe flinging hair into a brazier or dropping blood into a bowl of dark water. The Beast takes a -2 penalty to the next roll she makes to activate a Nightmare; in return, the Nightmare immediately takes effect on the target, provided that they are on the same plane of existence as the Beast and are within (Lair) miles, without a requirement for eye contact, touch or speech.<br /> <br /> <b>High Satiety:</b> The Beast's magic is profound, affecting the target even if they are on another plane of existence.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> With the expenditure of a point of Satiety, the Beast may choose to incorporate the sympathetic link into a small object - often a doll, but other forms are possible. The object may be used as a trigger for its Nightmare at a later point with a successful Intelligence + Satiety roll so long as it is held in the Beast's hand, and functions a number of times equal to the Beast's Lair before being destroyed, torn apart by some manifestation of dark magic - perhaps it bursts into flames or decays into a foul sludge. A failed roll still consumes a Nightmare 'charge'. If the doll is destroyed before all its Nightmares are used, the victim suffers one final Nightmare immediately, but the rest are lost.<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> As per the invoked Nightmare.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 03-11-2018, 08:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-11T05:17:44-07:00","id":1194215,"title":"","content":"That penalty seems a bit low for the extreme range, even considering you need a Sympathetic link. As is, this would be a must have Nightmare for any beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-11T05:22:08-07:00","id":1194217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=1194215#post1194215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That penalty seems a bit low for the extreme range, even considering you need a Sympathetic link. As is, this would be a must have Nightmare for any beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was my worry. Maybe impose a range of (Lair) miles?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-11T05:29:10-07:00","id":1194219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=1194217#post1194217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was my worry. Maybe impose a range of (Lair) miles?</div> </div> </div> </div>Might be better. Though you are using Mage and Sympathetic links for this, I can't help but feel it would be more thematic for the Beast to simply open up their usual Nightmare vectors via a conduit like mirrors, shadows, or finding the Target in dreams.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-11T05:34:23-07:00","id":1194221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=1194219#post1194219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Might be better. Though you are using Mage and Sympathetic links for this, I can't help but feel it would be more thematic for the Beast to simply open up their usual Nightmare vectors via a conduit like mirrors, shadows, or finding the Target in dreams.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, can you explain that a bit further? I'm not entirely sure what you mean.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-11T19:37:51-07:00","id":1194422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=1194221#post1194221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, can you explain that a bit further? I'm not entirely sure what you mean.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. Rather than the Mage-y &quot;burn lock of hair to target anywhere&quot;, i was thinking you either A) tag them with the Nightmare first, then can hit them with other Nightmares using the medium of nearby reflections, or shadows, or whatever, instead of your eyes - those things counts as your eyes, for the sake of Nightmare targeting. Or B) you &quot;hunt&quot; the Target through their Dreams, and hit them with Nightmares there.<br /> <br /> A is specific in its targeting, and likely to give them a phobia to whatever medium you are using for targeting. B can hit targets you've never directly seen, and likely to make them an insomniac.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-12T00:20:37-07:00","id":1194454,"title":"","content":"The &quot;Hunting through the mirror&quot; is very topical. I mean, just remember all those Horror movies where the monster is visible for a split second, the victim is shocked, turns around, and finds there is nothing there. Would make it more ghost-kinship, though, but whatever, cool is cool =D<br /> Instead of &quot;this happens now&quot;, it'd take place the next time the victim looks into a surface that can function as a mirror. Would be a slightly different nightmare, of course.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-12T00:30:31-07:00","id":1194456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=1194454#post1194454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The &quot;Hunting through the mirror&quot; is very topical. I mean, just remember all those Horror movies where the monster is visible for a split second, the victim is shocked, turns around, and finds there is nothing there. Would make it more ghost-kinship, though, but whatever, cool is cool =D<br /> Instead of &quot;this happens now&quot;, it'd take place the next time the victim looks into a surface that can function as a mirror. Would be a slightly different nightmare, of course.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ghost or Changeling would be appropriate.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking the normal effect is just a hallucination you set up to be triggered the next time the subject looks in a mirror. At High Satiety you don't have to set up the specifics in advance like that - instead the next time they look in a mirror, you become aware of it, can see them and can appear to them in the moment. With Satiety expenditure you can work additional Nightmares through the Mirror at that point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-12T00:39:51-07:00","id":1194458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=1194456#post1194456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ghost or Changeling would be appropriate.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking the normal effect is just a hallucination you set up to be triggered the next time the subject looks in a mirror. At High Satiety you don't have to set up the specifics in advance like that - instead the next time they look in a mirror, you become aware of it, can see them and can appear to them in the moment. With Satiety expenditure you can work additional Nightmares through the Mirror at that point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very Bloody Mary. Maybe the basic effect requires that they do something in front of the mirror, set when you use the nightmare?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-12T06:31:01-07:00","id":1194508,"title":"","content":"Hmm. What about one based on Sin-Eater Kinship (specifically Boneyard) that lets a Beast target Nightmares through a claimed area (easier than opening Primordial Pathways left-and-right).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-12T07:35:09-07:00","id":1194529,"title":"","content":"I had, funnily enough, forgotten that this thread existed, so I posted this originally over in the homebrew Atavism topic, since it complements something I wrote there. I think it should also be able to work on any sort of small comestible, despite the nomenclature.<br /> <br /> <b>Witch's Brew</b><br /> <br /> <i>Everyone knows this: Don't take candy from strangers. Don't leave your drink unattended. Don't accept that apple pie from your kindly neighbor. They could have put anything in it.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Normal Effect: </b>To use this Nightmare, the Beast must create or tamper with a beverage of some sort. This could take the form of brewing a foul-smelling liquid in a cauldron, mixing up a mojito, or merely stirring a packet of sugar into someone's coffee. The Beast takes a -2 penalty to the next roll she makes to activate a Nightmare; in return, the next person who imbibes the tampered beverage suffers its effects.<br /> <br /> <b>High Satiety:</b> The Beast can imbue a Nightmare into a number of drinks equal to her Lair.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> The Beast makes the drink especially tempting. This is the best cup of coffee her victim's ever smelled, or the Hero is convinced that this is a magical potion that will increase his might tenfold. The Beast can choose whether this effect applies to anyone, a single person of her designation, or other specified group in-between. A person who fits the criteria and who comes across the Nightmare-infused beverage must make a Resolve + Composure roll or immediately drink the beverage, downing it in one gulp if possible. Offering the drink to someone who fits the criteria always counts as Soft Leverage.<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> As per the invoked Nightmare.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-12T08:03:31-07:00","id":1194533,"title":"","content":"Have we had a 'You Are A Frog' Nightmare yet, one that causes the victim to hallucinate that they've been transformed into some kind of animal?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T06:15:03-07:00","id":1195251,"title":"","content":"I feel like the nightmare for hunting through mirrors should be a kinship for changelings.<br /> <br /> Edit: I didn't realize I'd lose an entire page in this discussion...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T12:54:13-07:00","id":1195430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArchonAres</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=1195251#post1195251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like the nightmare for hunting through mirrors should be a kinship for changelings.<br /> <br /> Edit: I didn't realize I'd lose an entire page in this discussion...</div> </div> </div> </div>Mirrors was an example. It could be other people, shadows, advertisements, etc. The idea was more: target identifies something as the Beast, the Beast uses a Nightmare through the thing. Eventual reaction: target becomes terrified of the thing.<br /> <br /> Hunting via dreams was a separate idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T08:24:43-07:00","id":1197205,"title":"","content":"Did we have a Nightmare that make victims unable to forget something?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T08:38:55-07:00","id":1197212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=1197205#post1197205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did we have a Nightmare that make victims unable to forget something?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not that I know of.<br /> <br /> Does anyone have any ideas for a Nightmare that allows the activation of Nightmares by 'attaching' them to animals, familiar-style?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T09:01:01-07:00","id":1197225,"title":"","content":"As slasher kinship is grossly unexplored, what would be some good Nightmares? Not only ones that represent what people have to fear from slashers, but the fears of ... how do I word this...becoming a slasher? Or what it's like to be a slasher?<br /> <br /> Only ones I can think of are just reskins of existing common nightmares","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T09:37:17-07:00","id":1197240,"title":"","content":"Something is wrong with you<br /> <br /> Effect: Victim has creepy urges every time a social roll fails, and needs to roll Resolve + composure or else give in to them. <br /> High satiety: Victim gains the disturbed condition (or something like that). Ethics and morality are abstract concepts that are hard to keep track of.<br /> sat expenditure: The Beast can change the victim's Aspirations and Vice to something creepy violent for the scene.<br /> Exceptional Success: All non-creepy rolls Suffer -2","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T09:49:36-07:00","id":1197243,"title":"","content":"Needs work, but I like it. I'll come back to it when I have more time","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T11:03:49-07:00","id":1197265,"title":"","content":"as an idea for Slashers: <br /> <b><i>You're The Bad Guy</i></b><br /> Basically the fear of quite simply being the bad guy. <i>And knowing it. </i>and yet at the same time not being able to stop or even reveling in it. It scares you, and you can't stop. no. you won't stop. and that's so much worse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13001-sdespencer","name":"SdeSpencer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T11:05:46-07:00","id":1197266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SdeSpencer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=1197265#post1197265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">as an idea for Slashers:<br /> <b><i>You're The Bad Guy</i></b><br /> Basically the fear of quite simply being the bad guy. <i>And knowing it. </i>and yet at the same time not being able to stop or even reveling in it. It scares you, and you can't stop. no. you won't stop. and that's so much worse.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a fear that the Beasts are very involved with as well, only they subvert it - to some degree, at least. Sounds like a good one to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T11:47:03-07:00","id":1197278,"title":"","content":"also, as a few other ideas (Reasonably i'd put all of these as kinship merits, but i don't know what to label them all as):<br /> <b><i>All Your Instincts are Wrong</i></b><br /> You feel that little scratching at the back of your head. it's telling you to do something. it's telling you it <i>knows</i> something. the voice, that feeling in your gut, that twitching of your finger, you know it to be dead wrong. it's telling you to do something self destructive or that you need to do something you'll regret. it's the little inchling telling you to put your hand in the fire because it's warm or to eat the detergent, it's just a fruit! You know it to be wrong but it just won't shake<br /> <br /> <b><i>Why Do You Hate Them</i><i>? </i></b><br /> Your Friend. Your Wife. Your Kid. Even this random stranger. You hate them with a passion. You don't know why or how or what and you certainly don't like it in the slightest. They did nothing wrong. they haven't changed even. But you <i>HATE THEM</i>. and you don't know why. maybe you'll kill them tomorrow morning. maybe today. maybe you could sneak to the kitchen and get a knife right now. NO NO. This is my Friend or my Family or just a random guy. They did nothing wrong. So why do you hate them so much? (this was originally conceived as a Hero Kinship, but the BPG informed us you cant really get kinships with Heroes. it might fit with Prometheans, but i'm not sure given the context)<br /> <br /> <i><b>You're A Fake (Fetch)</b></i><br /> Your the Fake. you might as well not exist. just a puppet meant to replace someone. and it eats you up inside and you don't know what to do with it besides be terrified and not able to handle any of it and how do you even talk to the real you when they come back for their life? What if they never do? Who even are you anymore, if you don't have a real claim to being you? Do you even matter? are you better off gone?<br /> <br /> <i><b>There's No Endgame (Pandoran)</b></i><br /> This is as good as it can get for you. and this sucks. you can't go up from here, and you're pretty sure that this is Reasonably Close to rock bottom. this isn't a life worth living, but there isn't anything better in death either. You're screwed as screwed can be. And there's no way out of any of it. How's it feel?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13001-sdespencer","name":"SdeSpencer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T12:51:34-07:00","id":1199156,"title":"","content":"Have we got a nightmare that causes memory loss, you know, following the &quot;too horrible to remember&quot; trope?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T13:05:55-07:00","id":1199160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=1199156#post1199156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have we got a nightmare that causes memory loss, you know, following the &amp;quot;too horrible to remember&amp;quot; trope?</div> </div> </div> </div>We've got Tabula Rasa from the corebook. You could reskin it and use Werewolf for a Kinship (because of Lunacy).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T22:05:38-07:00","id":1199300,"title":"","content":"So here's something.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\">You Cannot Forget</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><i><span style=\"font-size:13px\">They said that oblivion is a gift to the human mind. No, you will not enjoy that gift. Now that you know, you will never forget.</span></i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Dice Pool</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">: Intelligence + Satiety vs. Resolve + Supernatural Tolerance</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Normal</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">: An idea or information takes root in the victim's mind, and she can't get it out. She gains a non-persistent version of the Obsession Condition, where she becomes obsessed with preserving and spreading the knowledge. Also, the loss of 10-again also applies to any breaking point rolls or equivalents she suffers in pursuit of the obsession.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Unlike most Nightmares, this Nightmare requires not eye contact but speech as a vector.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b><span style=\"font-size:13px\">High Satiety</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">: The knowledge warps and spasms within the victim's mind, driving him to further fixation. He gains the Deprived Condition, where he is addicted to spreading the implanted information.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Satiety Expenditure</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">: The victim's mind gets chunks of it ripped out, replaced by the knowledge implanted by the Beast. Both the Obsession and Deprived Conditions become persistent. Furthermore, the knowledge cannot be removed by natural means. The victim will remember it clearly after decades, and neither old age nor brain damage affects it. This time-proof memory is independent of the inflicted Conditions. Curing them simply means she is not inhibited by the knowledge. Removing the memory via supernatural means triggers a Clash of Wills where the Beast rolls Intelligence + Satiety.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Exceptional Success</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">: The Beast is able to change what information the victim remembers and becomes obsessed with. He still needs to speak the knowledge to his victim, but does not need to roll.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T01:26:03-07:00","id":1209143,"title":"","content":"<u><b>You Cannot Stop</b></u><br /> <br /> <i>You have to keep going. You're nowhere near your limit. You cannot be. You have to keep going. Just until the next tree.... no, the one after that... the next one....</i><br /> <br /> Dice Pool: Manipulation + Satiety vs. Resolve + Supernatural Tolerance<br /> <br /> Normal: The victim becomes obsessed with a certain simple and repetitive action, doing it again and again - be it trying to dunk that ball for the 200th time, swim some more, run another mile, keep writing that same page, solving rubik's cubes again and again etc. The Victim gains a temporary Obsession of the player's choice, but it cannot be too out of character (a cook will not suddenly become obsessed with martial arts if he hadn't harbored an interest beforehand). For a scene, the obsession cannot be shed. The character takes moderate care of themselves, and stops when taking bashing damage due to the action.<br /> <br /> High Satiety: Obsession is one thing, being totally one-minded something else entirely - the victim gains 8-again on his Obsession. To attempt a roll not related to the obsession takes a Willpower.<br /> <br /> Satiety Expenditure: They victim completely disregards health and safety, and keeps repeating their obsession to the point of total collapse - they will write through night after night (just that one same page though, this is no cure for writer's block!), or keep running until their legs give in. Only the most minute distractions are tolerable. Taking lethal damage as a direct result of the action (e.g. falling due to failing to climb higher) ends the effect.<br /> (Think Forrest Gump-levels of 'I'll go run a bit')<br /> <br /> Exceptional Success: Even taking Lethal damage does not stop the character from repeating the action.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-11T04:06:49-07:00","id":1217613,"title":"","content":"<u><b>I Know Your Weakness!</b></u><br /> <br /> <i>You cannot match him - everytime you try something, he counters you, as if he'd known exactly what you would do. Why even try? You're just gonna get hurt...</i><br /> <br /> <b>Normal Effect: </b>The victim loses their Defense when opposing the Beast for a scene, and suffers a -2 penalty on attacking them for fear of being hit.<br /> <b>High Satiety: </b>The Beast may chose a different person to enjoy the benefits of this Nightmare instead. In addition, each time the victim takes more damage than their Composure, they have to roll Resolve+Composure or suffer Beaten Down.<br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure: </b>The victim suffers from a Delusion, believing even the Beast's slightest touch causes them tremendous pain and rips them to shreds, and reacts accordingly. The Beast and placeholder can cause Tilts like Leg Wrack and Arm Wrack with but a touch, even if otherwise this weren't possible: the arm is not really broken, but in the victim's mind it is, and thus they cannot use it. In addition, the victim's Stamina is considered to be 1 for purposes of inflicting Knockdown or similar.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success: </b>The penalty increases to -4.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-11T05:17:29-07:00","id":1217629,"title":"","content":"Not sure how it would work outside of perhaps somehow penalizing investigation, but You Can't Thwart Stage One sounds like a great name for a Nightmare. Then again, I love supervillain/shonen villain aesthetic for Beasts","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T09:17:28-07:00","id":1220556,"title":"","content":"<u><b>You Are a Tool (Wizened Changeling/Unfleshed Promethean/Princess Kinship)</b></u><br /> <br /> <i>Helping yourself is not only harder than helping others, it's immoral. You mean nothing except when you serve other, more important beings</i><br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool</b>: Manipulation + Satiety vs. Resolve + Supernatural Tolerance<br /> <br /> <b>Normal Effect</b>: Victim gets -3 dice to any action that involves helping only themselves. When assisting others in teamwork actions, the victim adds the appropriate skill dots as a straight equipment bonus instead of the usual teamwork roll.<br /> <b>High Satiety</b>: Victim gets Obsession(Doing my job) condition until the end of the scene, with &quot;job&quot; defined as either their Professional Training merit profession (if they have it) or their Specialty for the highest skill rating most integral to the character concept. This condition can never directly influence them towards doing something wholly suicidal or that would otherwise cause a breaking point<br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure</b>: Victim Gains the Thrall Condition, but it resolves at the end of the scene.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success</b>: Victim cannot move at all without either a successful Resolve + Composure roll for every action that takes up a whole turn or sensing an opportunity to help someone else, except to dodge incoming attacks (they keep their Defense). Additionally, at the end of the scene, the target will not remember anything that happened during that scene, for they as a person did not really take part in it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 05-20-2018, 02:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T10:12:35-07:00","id":1220565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=1220556#post1220556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u><b>You Are a Tool (Wizened Changeling/Unfleshed Promethean/Princess Kinship)</b></u><br /> <br /> <i>Helping yourself is not only harder than helping others, it's immoral. You mean nothing except when you serve other, more important beings</i><br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool</b>: (UNSURE) + Satiety vs. Resolve + Supernatural Tolerance<br /> <br /> <b>Normal Effect</b>: Victim gets -3 dice to any action that involves helping only themselves. When assisting others in teamwork actions, the victim adds the appropriate skill dots as a straight equipment bonus instead of the usual teamwork roll.<br /> <b>High Satiety</b>: Victim gets Obsession(Helping Beast with X) condition for any task that doesn't directly put them in immediate physical danger.<br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure</b>: Victim cannot move at all without either a successful Resolve + Composure roll for every action that takes up a whole turn or a direct order from anyone else on the scene, except to dodge incoming attacks (they keep their Defense). Additionally, at the end of the scene, the target will not remember anything that happened during that scene, for they as a person did not really take part in it.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success</b>: Penalty to acting alone increases to -5, add +1 to all &quot;equipment bonuses&quot;<br /> <br /> EDIT: I need a better Exceptional Success</div> </div> </div> </div>For the Attribute in the dice pool, I think Manipulation is the best. You don't become a tool by being ordered into it, you become a tool by the slow grinding-down and usurpation of your own wants and needs by those of your user. As for the Exceptional Success, I think that maybe you could do something with the victim intuiting the desires of their 'master(s)' without even needing to be told.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T10:19:43-07:00","id":1220566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=1220565#post1220565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For the Attribute in the dice pool, I think Manipulation is the best. You don't become a tool by being ordered into it, you become a tool by the slow grinding-down and usurpation of your own wants and needs by those of your user. As for the Exceptional Success, I think that maybe you could do something with the victim intuiting the desires of their 'master(s)' without even needing to be told.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That exceptional success sounds like a good idea, but I'm stumped on how to translate that concept into good mechanics. Any ideas?<br /> <br /> Oh, and yeah, it's definitely Master<b><i><u>s</u></i></b> to separate it conceptually from You Must Obey. You're not just a slave with this power, you're not even a person. It's not that this Beast is your superior, you are just everyone else's inferior","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 05-20-2018, 01:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T10:21:40-07:00","id":1220568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=1220566#post1220566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The exception success sounds like a good idea, but I'm stumped on how to translate that concept into good mechanics. Any ideas?</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps if another character in the scene wants something, the victim gets an Empathy roll with some bonus to notice the need and intuit it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T10:24:47-07:00","id":1220571,"title":"","content":"I'm beginning to realize just how horrifying this Nightmare is, especially in conjunction with something like this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=542048#post542048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>You Can't Quit Me</b>(Daeva)<br /> <br /> <i>You want to get away, to never see them again. But then they smile and whisper in your ear, and your heart turns in your chest and the wonderful warmth spreads through your flesh, and you know, deep down inside, that you'll never leave them, no matter how badly they hurt you.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Manipulation + Satiety vs Resolve + Supernatural Tolerance<br /> <br /> <b>Normal:</b> The victim gains the Swooning Condition (p. XX) keyed towards the Beast, and cannot resolve it during the scene, no matter how many times they bend to the Child's will. After the scene ends, the Condition may be resolved normally.<br /> <br /> <b>High Satiety:</b> As normal, save that the Beast treats their Impression level as two higher against the afflicted target, to a maximum of perfect(see p. XX).<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> The victim gains the Addicted(Persistent) Condition (p. XX) ,which does not resolve when the Nightmare ends and is keyed towards acts of kindness and affirmation(A kiss on the cheek, warm praise, a soft smile, anything of that sort will do) from the user.*<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> When resisting the user's mundane Social rolls, the victim gains an Exceptional Success on 6 Successes instead of 5.<br /> <br /> So, what do you think?</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T10:26:03-07:00","id":1220572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=1220571#post1220571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm beginning to realize just how horrifying this Nightmare is, especially in conjunction with something like this:<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Unlimited You Must Obey? Is this a balance problem or a feature? I'm pretty sure even with both though, you couldn't get them to do anything too dangerous. More complex orders than You Must Obey, but not as immediately suicidal orders. A Beast with all three is basically The Purple Man though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 05-20-2018, 01:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T10:31:15-07:00","id":1220574,"title":"","content":"Oh wow. I forgot to put in that Obsession is non-persistent. The Obsession is only supposed to last until the end of the scene.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T10:52:09-07:00","id":1220579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=1220572#post1220572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Unlimited You Must Obey? Is this a balance problem or a feature? I'm pretty sure even with both though, you couldn't get them to do anything too dangerous. More complex orders than You Must Obey, but not as immediately suicidal orders. A Beast with all three is basically The Purple Man though.</div> </div> </div> </div>A feature, I think, although I do think you should A) make it clear that the victim won't do directly suicidal things, maybe not even things which would cause a Breaking Point and B) perhaps any idea of giving the victim direct orders should be removed? They're a tool, after all. You don't need to order them, they <i>just do their job</i>. They don't work outside it, don't try to find something else to do and don't try new things - they're a tool, a machine, that <i>does their job</i>, head down and blinkers firmly on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T10:53:21-07:00","id":1220580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=1220566#post1220566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That exceptional success sounds like a good idea, but I'm stumped on how to translate that concept into good mechanics. Any ideas?<br /> <br /> Oh, and yeah, it's definitely Master<b><i><u>s</u></i></b> to separate it conceptually from You Must Obey. You're not just a slave with this power, you're not even a person. It's not that this Beast is your superior, you are just everyone else's inferior</div> </div> </div> </div>What about leveraging the Thrall Condition (typically from the full onset of Soullessness, but it seems applicable here, as a temporary thing)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T10:55:06-07:00","id":1220581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=1220580#post1220580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What about leveraging the Thrall Condition (typically from the full onset of Soullessness, but it seems applicable here, as a temporary thing)?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a good idea. We've already got a Nightmare that inflicts Soullessness, IIRC, though I can't remember the name and don't have <i>Beast</i> to hand. Maybe we could borrow from that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T11:06:06-07:00","id":1220583,"title":"","content":"On the topic of &quot;villainous&quot; Nightmares, is there already something like &quot;Do Not Fail Me (Again)&quot; to goad minions into greater heights of focus (albeit at some other cost)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T11:52:24-07:00","id":1220594,"title":"","content":"I made the original Satiety Expenditure Effect the new Exceptional Success effect and made temporary Thralldom the Satiety Expenditure effect. What do y'all think? also, where would i find the effects of the Thrall condition? Please tell me it's not in Mage 2e? I don't want to buy more books.<br /> <br /> Also changed the Obsession to &quot;Doing My Job&quot;, though the definition of job might be too complicated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T11:54:07-07:00","id":1220596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=1220583#post1220583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the topic of &quot;villainous&quot; Nightmares, is there already something like &quot;Do Not Fail Me (Again)&quot; to goad minions into greater heights of focus (albeit at some other cost)?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I love villainous Nightmares, but I feel like Terror's Friend and a lot of existing Nightmares can achieve something like that already.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T12:00:45-07:00","id":1220598,"title":"","content":"was thinking a nightmare that could be used on a place or person if you find out it's dangerous or that a person is a child molestor, serial killer, RIAA employee, etc.<br /> <br /> one that pre emptively protect people from going to the dangerous place or trusting the dangerous person.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T12:14:18-07:00","id":1220603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=556499#post556499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No One Walks Here (hunters in darkness) - imbues a location with a fearsome aura that creates rumors guaranteeing MOST people won't dare violate your territory.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> We could expand this for your idea, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1153\" data-vbnamecard=\"1153\">Prince of the Night</a>. I gotta be honest though, i can't see Beasts doing this. They're not the type to put up a fence at the cliff edge. They teach through direct experience. In the fence at the cliff edge example, they'll be like Canadians, who instead put up a sign listing how many people died falling off that cliff in the last couple of years and let you decide if the thrill is worth it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 05-20-2018, 03:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T13:54:56-07:00","id":1220616,"title":"","content":"We got delayed, contagious, and repeating nightmare modifiers. We got blood as a carrier, and planting them in a room beforehand. I don't see why there shouldnt be a way to cast a nightmare 'through' someone else.<br /> would help loads in isolating that person socially.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T15:12:18-07:00","id":1220633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=1220616#post1220616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We got delayed, contagious, and repeating nightmare modifiers. We got blood as a carrier, and planting them in a room beforehand. I don't see why there shouldnt be a way to cast a nightmare 'through' someone else.<br /> would help loads in isolating that person socially.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't that what Fear is Contagious does already?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T17:11:09-07:00","id":1220662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=1220594#post1220594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">also, where would i find the effects of the Thrall condition? Please tell me it's not in Mage 2e? I don't want to buy more books.</div> </div> </div> </div>Looks like? It shouldn't be, since Soullessness is pretty common/core.<br /> <br /> Summary of the effects: No Willpower spending, no Defense, can't spend XP (negligible for a single scene), Broken Condition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T20:14:24-07:00","id":1220695,"title":"","content":"Hmm. Now I'm not sure how appropriate it is for this Nightmare. I could be convinced though","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T03:08:52-07:00","id":1220772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=1220633#post1220633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Isn't that what Fear is Contagious does already?</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically yes, but the Victim suffers the Nightmare, too. I was thinking of a 'Marked as an Outcast' Kind of thing. Weirdness Magnet - shit happens to people when they are around, but they are not affected themselves","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T04:14:43-07:00","id":1220781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Urbenmyth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=1070997#post1070997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>You Are Feared (Common)</b><br /> <i>Look at you. Beaten down, cowering, fleeing from monsters on all sides. Don't you wish you knew what it was like to be the powerful one, to be the terrible thing that the weak quiver and weep at the sight of?<br /> Here. Let it never be said monsters cannot be kind.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Roll</b>- As base nightmare (see below)<br /> <br /> <b>Normal Effect</b>- The beast uses another nightmare on the target, with a -2 penalty. If it succeeds, the &quot;victim&quot; gains the ability to use that nightmare for the rest of the scene.The victim can only use the normal effect, and must pay either a willpower point or 2 supernatural fuel points to use the nightmare. Beyond their store of these resources, there is no limit to how often they can use it. The manifestation of the nightmare remain the same as the original beast's, but the beast has no control over how the victim uses their new power, and cannot remove it prematurely.<br /> This nightmare cannot be used on another beast<br /> <br /> <b>High Satiety</b>- The victim uses the nightmare as if at high satiety (this effect remains even if the beast drops in satiety before the nightmare runs out)<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure</b>- The victim can spend double (i.e. two willpower or 4 supernatural fuel points) to use the nightmare's satiety expenditure effect.<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success</b>- The beast is immune to the victim's nightmare, and can make a contested resolve+supernatural resistance to preemptively remove the power if they wish.</div> </div> </div> </div>This could sort of work, though they would have to do it to themselves<br /> <br /> This doesn't say if the &quot;victim&quot; rolls for it or what, but i want to say it would be cool if they rolled the Beast's standard pool as it was when the Nightmare was activated. I might also extend it until sundown or sunrise, whichever comes first.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 05